{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4f6844c0-3b82-41b2-99e4-abe62041f502","agentId":"a7f5dba9e9d416cc6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers. Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no COM3; read MES logs read-only from the configured MES log dir (the mes catalog). Report under 150 words. Others own CSS, job/report/code templates, jobs_bridge, dossier_bridge/open-work builders: do not edit those. You own NEW docs/vehicles/ZASFAKPN5J7B88115/sessions/2026-10-14-morning-mes-scan.md, cuore/services/mes_handoff_bridge.py (import path only, additive), cuore/tests/check_mes_handoff.py (extend). You may commit and push (`github` main only; never koch-mcp/).\n\nMES wrote a real all-systems scan this morning: SCAN_2610140859.txt (2026-10-14 08:59) containing P0440/P0455 (per another agent). 1. Read it with the mes library (parse_scan_text / catalog) and write the session note: every module answered, every code with its failure-type byte and status wording as MES printed it, software/hardware numbers (compare with the 8 Oct scan: any module software change?), and a comparison table against the 13 Oct 20:03 live read (stored/pending/permanent from the car) and the 8 Oct 09:20 clear: which codes returned, which did not, which are new; note whether MES cleared anything this morning (search the file for CLEARING) — if it did, say so plainly and what that does to the readiness/verdict picture (a clear resets monitors; the EVAP monitor must run again before any verification). 2. Import it through the MES-import path (mes_handoff_bridge.import_mes_log) so it appears in the Scans timeline as source MES with its health line, and confirm /api/scans and the health report see it (TestClient, temp CUORE_STATE_DIR seeded with copies — never modify production files; then ALSO run the import against the production state dir once, since this is real car data the owner wants kept: C:\\ProgramData\\cuore — append only). 3. Extend check_mes_handoff.py with the real file as fixture (copied to a temp MES root): codes list and the health line. Run check_mes_handoff.py and check_scanlog.py only. Commit \"Morning MES scan 2026-10-14 ingested and compared with the 13 Oct live read\" with the Co-Authored-By line, push, report hash and the comparison table."},"uuid":"84287312-31f3-4328-b99b-ea68e91dfb98","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:58:35.136Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
