{"parentUuid":"f9c1e459-1bc1-4ec7-a47a-df30de41020f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7f5dba9e9d416cc6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2QWJkS6g9oEhLetv2bB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YCuPeqkCpHmbprUy1P4fbd","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\mes_handoff_bridge.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9003,"cache_read_input_tokens":57019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9003,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YCuPeqkCpHmbprUy1P4fbd":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\mes_handoff_bridge.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"58723456-c990-452f-99b1-657b43873c16","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg2QWJVYr7DziFqH7AZXp","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"bf4a48f4-8822-4f3c-90e9-b697a2fb5200","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:58:46.703Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"bf4a48f4-8822-4f3c-90e9-b697a2fb5200","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4f6844c0-3b82-41b2-99e4-abe62041f502","agentId":"a7f5dba9e9d416cc6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YCuPeqkCpHmbprUy1P4fbd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"MES handoff: the parts of a diagnosis CUORE deliberately never does over\n2\tHTTP (an actuator command, an adjustment, a coding write) because CUORE\n3\tnever writes to the car outside the consent-gated MCP path. For those, this\n4\tmodule hands the technician a card -- \"do this in MES: module, menu path,\n5\tprerequisites\" -- built from the sourced knowledge table in\n6\t:mod:`mes.mes_functions`.\n7\t\n8\tTwo things live here, both additive and read-mostly:\n9\t\n10\t1. **Handoff lookup** (:func:`candidates`, :func:`find_for_text`,\n11\t  :func:`card`) -- the Tests page and the job page's step 6 already have a\n12\t  pass/fail or done/outcome form for recording what happened; this module\n13\t  never duplicates that store (:mod:`cuore.live.checklists`). It only\n14\t  supplies the \"what to do in MES first\" text those existing forms sit\n15\t  below, matched against a test id or free-text step label.\n16\t\n17\t2. **MES log import** (:func:`import_mes_log`, :func:`list_mes_scans`) --\n18\t  point 4 of the 2026-10-14 pass: an MES SCAN/FES log that was captured\n19\t  outside CUORE's own live link (``cuore.live.scanlog``, which only ever\n20\t  clusters ``observations.jsonl`` -- an append-only record of what CUORE's\n21\t  own serial link actually read, never edited here) should still get a\n22\t  health report. Rather than disguise an MES-captured file as a live serial\n23\t  read (which ``cuore.live.store.is_from_car`` -- rightly -- would reject,\n24\t  and which would be dishonest about provenance even if it didn't), this\n25\t  keeps its own small, clearly-labelled ledger of MES-sourced scans\n26\t  (``mes_imports.json`` beside the other small JSON stores in\n27\t  :mod:`cuore.live.config`'s state dir) and computes the same verdict\n28\t  :mod:`mes.scan_health` would compute for a live one, via that module's\n29\t  own public :func:`mes.scan_health.verdict` -- never a second copy of its\n30\t  logic, and never a write to ``cuore.live.scanlog``'s or\n31\t  ``cuore.services.scan_health_bridge``'s own files.\n32\t\"\"\"\n33\t\n34\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n35\t\n36\timport json\n37\timport threading\n38\tfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n39\tfrom pathlib import Path\n40\tfrom typing import Any, Optional\n41\t\n42\tfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\n43\tfrom ..live.config import state_dir\n44\tfrom .errors import BadRequest, NotFound\n45\t\n46\tfrom mes import mes_functions  # noqa: E402\n47\tfrom mes import paths as mes_paths  # noqa: E402\n48\tfrom mes import scan as scan_mod  # noqa: E402\n49\tfrom mes import scan_health  # noqa: E402\n50\t\n51\ttry:\n52\t    from mes import fes as fes_mod  # noqa: E402\n53\texcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- FES import is a nice-to-have, not required\n54\t    fes_mod = None\n55\t\n56\t_LOCK = threading.Lock()\n57\t\n58\t\n59\t# ===========================================================================\n60\t# 1. Handoff cards\n61\t# ===========================================================================\n62\t\n63\tdef candidates() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n64\t    \"\"\"Every catalogued MES function, as full handoff cards plus the\n65\t    ``test_id`` cross-reference (when it has one). Small (well under 30\n66\t    rows) -- the Tests page and job page fetch this once and match\n67\t    client-side against the test id / step text already in the DOM\n68\t    (``_mes_handoff.html``'s own script), rather than round-tripping once\n69\t    per row/step.\"\"\"\n70\t    return [{**_render_card(f), \"test_id\": f[\"test_id\"]}\n71\t           for f in mes_functions.all_functions()]\n72\t\n73\t\n74\tdef card(function_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n75\t    \"\"\"The full handoff card for one function id. Raises :class:`NotFound`\n76\t    for an unknown id.\"\"\"\n77\t    f = mes_functions.function(function_id)\n78\t    if f is None:\n79\t        raise NotFound(f\"unknown MES function id {function_id!r}\")\n80\t    return _render_card(f)\n81\t\n82\t\n83\tdef _render_card(f: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n84\t    native = f[\"mes_support\"].startswith(\"no\")\n85\t    return {\n86\t        \"id\": f[\"id\"],\n87\t        \"title\": f\"Do this in {'the car' if native else 'MES'}: \"\n88\t                f\"{f['module']} -> {f['menu_path'].split(' -- ')[0]}\",\n89\t        \"module\": f[\"module\"],\n90\t        \"kind\": f[\"kind\"],\n91\t        \"name\": f[\"name\"],\n92\t        \"menu_path\": f[\"menu_path\"],\n93\t        \"cable\": f[\"cable\"],\n94\t        \"prerequisites\": f[\"prerequisites\"],\n95\t        \"record_after\": f[\"record_after\"],\n96\t        \"log_expected\": f[\"log_expected\"],\n97\t        \"mes_support\": f[\"mes_support\"],\n98\t        \"cuore_today\": f[\"cuore_today\"],\n99\t        \"source\": f[\"source\"],\n100\t        \"confidence\": f[\"confidence\"],\n101\t        \"notes\": f[\"notes\"],\n102\t        #: Never true for a handoff card -- restated here (not just in the\n103\t        #: docstring) so a client can assert on it directly.\n104\t        \"writes_to_car\": False,\n105\t    }\n106\t\n107\t\n108\tdef find_for_test(test_id: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n109\t    \"\"\"The handoff card for a mechanic-test catalogue id (``tests.html``'s\n110\t    own ``t.id``), or ``None`` when that test has no MES-only counterpart.\"\"\"\n111\t    hits = mes_functions.functions_for_test(test_id)\n112\t    return _render_card(hits[0]) if hits else None\n113\t\n114\t\n115\tdef find_for_text(text: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n116\t    \"\"\"The handoff card matching a free-text job step label (``job.html``'s\n117\t    checklist step text), or ``None``. First match wins -- the knowledge\n118\t    table has no two functions with overlapping names.\"\"\"\n119\t    hits = mes_functions.search(text)\n120\t    return _render_card(hits[0]) if hits else None\n121\t\n122\t\n123\t# ===========================================================================\n124\t# 2. MES log import -> a \"Scans\" entry CUORE didn't capture live\n125\t# ===========================================================================\n126\t\n127\tdef _ledger_path() -> Path:\n128\t    return state_dir() / \"mes_imports.json\"\n129\t\n130\t\n131\tdef _load_ledger() -> dict[str, Any]:\n132\t    try:\n133\t        return json.loads(_ledger_path().read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n134\t    except (OSError, ValueError):\n135\t        return {}\n136\t\n137\t\n138\tdef _save_ledger(data: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n139\t    try:\n140\t        _ledger_path().write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n141\t    except OSError:\n142\t        pass\n143\t\n144\t\n145\tdef _resolve_import(name: str) -> Path:\n146\t    try:\n147\t        return mes_paths.resolve_log(name)\n148\t    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 -- MesNotFound/MesPathError -> BadRequest\n149\t        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n150\t\n151\t\n152\tdef _dtc_codes(dtcs: list[Any]) -> list[str]:\n153\t    return [d.full for d in dtcs]\n154\t\n155\t\n156\tdef _scan_from_log(name: str, path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n157\t    \"\"\"A scan-shaped dict (same spirit as ``cuore.live.scanlog``'s own\n158\t    cluster shape -- id/vin/ecus/dtcs/source -- but built from a parsed MES\n159\t    file, never from ``observations.jsonl``) plus this scan's health\n160\t    verdict, computed via :func:`mes.scan_health.verdict` (that module's own\n161\t    public function, called -- never re-implemented).\"\"\"\n162\t    kind, raw_ts, _vehicle = mes_paths.classify_name(name)\n163\t    if kind == \"scan\":\n164\t        log = scan_mod.load_scan(path)\n165\t        vin = log.vin\n166\t        ecus = sorted({e.iso_code or e.name for e in log.modules})\n167\t        stored_codes = _dtc_codes(log.all_dtcs)\n168\t        simulation_note = log.provenance\n169\t    elif kind == \"fes\" and fes_mod is not None:\n170\t        log = fes_mod.load_fes(path)\n171\t        vin = log.vin\n172\t        ecus = sorted({n for _k, n in log.nodes}) or ([log.ecu_description]\n173\t                                                      if log.ecu_description else [])\n174\t        stored_codes = _dtc_codes(log.stored)\n175\t        simulation_note = (\"simulation\" if log.simulation else \"not flagged \"\n176\t                           \"as a simulation\")\n177\t    else:\n178\t        raise BadRequest(f\"{name!r} is not a recognised MES SCAN/FES log name\")\n179\t\n180\t    verdict = scan_health.verdict(stored=stored_codes)\n181\t    scan_id = f\"{'SCAN' if kind == 'scan' else 'FES'}_{raw_ts or 'import'}\"\n182\t    return {\n183\t        \"id\": scan_id,\n184\t        \"vin\": vin,\n185\t        \"ecus\": ecus,\n186\t        \"dtcs\": {\"stored\": stored_codes, \"pending\": [], \"permanent\": []},\n187\t        \"source\": {\"kind\": \"MES\", \"file\": name, \"provenance\": simulation_note},\n188\t        \"imported_at\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\"),\n189\t        \"health\": verdict,\n190\t    }\n191\t\n192\t\n193\tdef import_mes_log(vin: str, name: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n194\t    \"\"\"Parse an MES SCAN/FES log already on one of ``mes.paths``'s\n195\t    configured roots (the catalogue \"already rescans\" -- this just reads\n196\t    the one file named, the same containment-safe way every other MES log\n197\t    read in this repo does, via :func:`mes.paths.resolve_log`) and record\n198\t    it as a \"Scans timeline\" entry tagged ``source: \"MES\"``, with the same\n199\t    health verdict a CUORE live scan would get.\n200\t\n201\t    Raises :class:`BadRequest` for a VIN mismatch (never silently files an\n202\t    import under the wrong car) or an unrecognised log name/kind.\n203\t    \"\"\"\n204\t    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n205\t    if not vin:\n206\t        raise BadRequest(\"a VIN is required\")\n207\t    path = _resolve_import(name)\n208\t    scan = _scan_from_log(name, path)\n209\t    if scan[\"vin\"] and scan[\"vin\"] != vin:\n210\t        raise BadRequest(f\"{name!r} is for VIN {scan['vin']!r}, not {vin!r}\")\n211\t    scan[\"vin\"] = vin\n212\t    with _LOCK:\n213\t        data = _load_ledger()\n214\t        entries = data.setdefault(vin, [])\n215\t        entries = [e for e in entries if e[\"id\"] != scan[\"id\"]]  # re-import replaces\n216\t        entries.append(scan)\n217\t        entries.sort(key=lambda e: e.get(\"imported_at\") or \"\", reverse=True)\n218\t        data[vin] = entries\n219\t        _save_ledger(data)\n220\t    return scan\n221\t\n222\t\n223\tdef list_mes_scans(vin: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n224\t    \"\"\"Every MES-imported scan on file for this VIN, newest first -- the\n225\t    \"Scans timeline, source MES\" surface this pass adds. Additive to (never\n226\t    merged into) ``cuore.live.scanlog.list_scans``, which stays exactly what\n227\t    it has always been: CUORE's own live-link history.\"\"\"\n228\t    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n229\t    if not vin:\n230\t        return []\n231\t    with _LOCK:\n232\t        return list(_load_ledger().get(vin, []))\n233\t\n234\t\n235\tdef health_line(scan: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n236\t    \"\"\"One printable line for a handoff card's \"Import the MES log\" result\n237\t    -- ``build_verdict``'s own label plus its first basis sentence.\"\"\"\n238\t    v = scan.get(\"health\") or {}\n239\t    basis = v.get(\"basis\") or []\n240\t    label = v.get(\"label\") or \"no verdict\"\n241\t    return f\"{label}: {basis[0]}\" if basis else label\n242\t\n243\t\n244\t__all__ = [\"candidates\", \"card\", \"find_for_test\", \"find_for_text\",\n245\t          \"import_mes_log\", \"list_mes_scans\", \"health_line\"]\n246\t"}]},"uuid":"7bb2d4d6-00d4-4dfd-a6dc-64eda29d6ef5","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:58:46.762Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\services\\mes_handoff_bridge.py","content":"\"\"\"MES handoff: the parts of a diagnosis CUORE deliberately never does over\nHTTP (an actuator command, an adjustment, a coding write) because CUORE\nnever writes to the car outside the consent-gated MCP path. For those, this\nmodule hands the technician a card -- \"do this in MES: module, menu path,\nprerequisites\" -- built from the sourced knowledge table in\n:mod:`mes.mes_functions`.\n\nTwo things live here, both additive and read-mostly:\n\n1. **Handoff lookup** (:func:`candidates`, :func:`find_for_text`,\n  :func:`card`) -- the Tests page and the job page's step 6 already have a\n  pass/fail or done/outcome form for recording what happened; this module\n  never duplicates that store (:mod:`cuore.live.checklists`). It only\n  supplies the \"what to do in MES first\" text those existing forms sit\n  below, matched against a test id or free-text step label.\n\n2. **MES log import** (:func:`import_mes_log`, :func:`list_mes_scans`) --\n  point 4 of the 2026-10-14 pass: an MES SCAN/FES log that was captured\n  outside CUORE's own live link (``cuore.live.scanlog``, which only ever\n  clusters ``observations.jsonl`` -- an append-only record of what CUORE's\n  own serial link actually read, never edited here) should still get a\n  health report. Rather than disguise an MES-captured file as a live serial\n  read (which ``cuore.live.store.is_from_car`` -- rightly -- would reject,\n  and which would be dishonest about provenance even if it didn't), this\n  keeps its own small, clearly-labelled ledger of MES-sourced scans\n  (``mes_imports.json`` beside the other small JSON stores in\n  :mod:`cuore.live.config`'s state dir) and computes the same verdict\n  :mod:`mes.scan_health` would compute for a live one, via that module's\n  own public :func:`mes.scan_health.verdict` -- never a second copy of its\n  logic, and never a write to ``cuore.live.scanlog``'s or\n  ``cuore.services.scan_health_bridge``'s own files.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport threading\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Optional\n\nfrom .. import bootstrap  # noqa: F401  -- side effect: puts `mes` on sys.path\nfrom ..live.config import state_dir\nfrom .errors import BadRequest, NotFound\n\nfrom mes import mes_functions  # noqa: E402\nfrom mes import paths as mes_paths  # noqa: E402\nfrom mes import scan as scan_mod  # noqa: E402\nfrom mes import scan_health  # noqa: E402\n\ntry:\n    from mes import fes as fes_mod  # noqa: E402\nexcept Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 -- FES import is a nice-to-have, not required\n    fes_mod = None\n\n_LOCK = threading.Lock()\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 1. Handoff cards\n# ===========================================================================\n\ndef candidates() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every catalogued MES function, as full handoff cards plus the\n    ``test_id`` cross-reference (when it has one). Small (well under 30\n    rows) -- the Tests page and job page fetch this once and match\n    client-side against the test id / step text already in the DOM\n    (``_mes_handoff.html``'s own script), rather than round-tripping once\n    per row/step.\"\"\"\n    return [{**_render_card(f), \"test_id\": f[\"test_id\"]}\n           for f in mes_functions.all_functions()]\n\n\ndef card(function_id: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"The full handoff card for one function id. Raises :class:`NotFound`\n    for an unknown id.\"\"\"\n    f = mes_functions.function(function_id)\n    if f is None:\n        raise NotFound(f\"unknown MES function id {function_id!r}\")\n    return _render_card(f)\n\n\ndef _render_card(f: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    native = f[\"mes_support\"].startswith(\"no\")\n    return {\n        \"id\": f[\"id\"],\n        \"title\": f\"Do this in {'the car' if native else 'MES'}: \"\n                f\"{f['module']} -> {f['menu_path'].split(' -- ')[0]}\",\n        \"module\": f[\"module\"],\n        \"kind\": f[\"kind\"],\n        \"name\": f[\"name\"],\n        \"menu_path\": f[\"menu_path\"],\n        \"cable\": f[\"cable\"],\n        \"prerequisites\": f[\"prerequisites\"],\n        \"record_after\": f[\"record_after\"],\n        \"log_expected\": f[\"log_expected\"],\n        \"mes_support\": f[\"mes_support\"],\n        \"cuore_today\": f[\"cuore_today\"],\n        \"source\": f[\"source\"],\n        \"confidence\": f[\"confidence\"],\n        \"notes\": f[\"notes\"],\n        #: Never true for a handoff card -- restated here (not just in the\n        #: docstring) so a client can assert on it directly.\n        \"writes_to_car\": False,\n    }\n\n\ndef find_for_test(test_id: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"The handoff card for a mechanic-test catalogue id (``tests.html``'s\n    own ``t.id``), or ``None`` when that test has no MES-only counterpart.\"\"\"\n    hits = mes_functions.functions_for_test(test_id)\n    return _render_card(hits[0]) if hits else None\n\n\ndef find_for_text(text: str) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"The handoff card matching a free-text job step label (``job.html``'s\n    checklist step text), or ``None``. First match wins -- the knowledge\n    table has no two functions with overlapping names.\"\"\"\n    hits = mes_functions.search(text)\n    return _render_card(hits[0]) if hits else None\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 2. MES log import -> a \"Scans\" entry CUORE didn't capture live\n# ===========================================================================\n\ndef _ledger_path() -> Path:\n    return state_dir() / \"mes_imports.json\"\n\n\ndef _load_ledger() -> dict[str, Any]:\n    try:\n        return json.loads(_ledger_path().read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except (OSError, ValueError):\n        return {}\n\n\ndef _save_ledger(data: dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    try:\n        _ledger_path().write_text(json.dumps(data, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    except OSError:\n        pass\n\n\ndef _resolve_import(name: str) -> Path:\n    try:\n        return mes_paths.resolve_log(name)\n    except Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001 -- MesNotFound/MesPathError -> BadRequest\n        raise BadRequest(str(exc)) from exc\n\n\ndef _dtc_codes(dtcs: list[Any]) -> list[str]:\n    return [d.full for d in dtcs]\n\n\ndef _scan_from_log(name: str, path: Path) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"A scan-shaped dict (same spirit as ``cuore.live.scanlog``'s own\n    cluster shape -- id/vin/ecus/dtcs/source -- but built from a parsed MES\n    file, never from ``observations.jsonl``) plus this scan's health\n    verdict, computed via :func:`mes.scan_health.verdict` (that module's own\n    public function, called -- never re-implemented).\"\"\"\n    kind, raw_ts, _vehicle = mes_paths.classify_name(name)\n    if kind == \"scan\":\n        log = scan_mod.load_scan(path)\n        vin = log.vin\n        ecus = sorted({e.iso_code or e.name for e in log.modules})\n        stored_codes = _dtc_codes(log.all_dtcs)\n        simulation_note = log.provenance\n    elif kind == \"fes\" and fes_mod is not None:\n        log = fes_mod.load_fes(path)\n        vin = log.vin\n        ecus = sorted({n for _k, n in log.nodes}) or ([log.ecu_description]\n                                                      if log.ecu_description else [])\n        stored_codes = _dtc_codes(log.stored)\n        simulation_note = (\"simulation\" if log.simulation else \"not flagged \"\n                           \"as a simulation\")\n    else:\n        raise BadRequest(f\"{name!r} is not a recognised MES SCAN/FES log name\")\n\n    verdict = scan_health.verdict(stored=stored_codes)\n    scan_id = f\"{'SCAN' if kind == 'scan' else 'FES'}_{raw_ts or 'import'}\"\n    return {\n        \"id\": scan_id,\n        \"vin\": vin,\n        \"ecus\": ecus,\n        \"dtcs\": {\"stored\": stored_codes, \"pending\": [], \"permanent\": []},\n        \"source\": {\"kind\": \"MES\", \"file\": name, \"provenance\": simulation_note},\n        \"imported_at\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\"),\n        \"health\": verdict,\n    }\n\n\ndef import_mes_log(vin: str, name: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Parse an MES SCAN/FES log already on one of ``mes.paths``'s\n    configured roots (the catalogue \"already rescans\" -- this just reads\n    the one file named, the same containment-safe way every other MES log\n    read in this repo does, via :func:`mes.paths.resolve_log`) and record\n    it as a \"Scans timeline\" entry tagged ``source: \"MES\"``, with the same\n    health verdict a CUORE live scan would get.\n\n    Raises :class:`BadRequest` for a VIN mismatch (never silently files an\n    import under the wrong car) or an unrecognised log name/kind.\n    \"\"\"\n    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n    if not vin:\n        raise BadRequest(\"a VIN is required\")\n    path = _resolve_import(name)\n    scan = _scan_from_log(name, path)\n    if scan[\"vin\"] and scan[\"vin\"] != vin:\n        raise BadRequest(f\"{name!r} is for VIN {scan['vin']!r}, not {vin!r}\")\n    scan[\"vin\"] = vin\n    with _LOCK:\n        data = _load_ledger()\n        entries = data.setdefault(vin, [])\n        entries = [e for e in entries if e[\"id\"] != scan[\"id\"]]  # re-import replaces\n        entries.append(scan)\n        entries.sort(key=lambda e: e.get(\"imported_at\") or \"\", reverse=True)\n        data[vin] = entries\n        _save_ledger(data)\n    return scan\n\n\ndef list_mes_scans(vin: str) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Every MES-imported scan on file for this VIN, newest first -- the\n    \"Scans timeline, source MES\" surface this pass adds. Additive to (never\n    merged into) ``cuore.live.scanlog.list_scans``, which stays exactly what\n    it has always been: CUORE's own live-link history.\"\"\"\n    vin = (vin or \"\").strip()\n    if not vin:\n        return []\n    with _LOCK:\n        return list(_load_ledger().get(vin, []))\n\n\ndef health_line(scan: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"One printable line for a handoff card's \"Import the MES log\" result\n    -- ``build_verdict``'s own label plus its first basis sentence.\"\"\"\n    v = scan.get(\"health\") or {}\n    basis = v.get(\"basis\") or []\n    label = v.get(\"label\") or \"no verdict\"\n    return f\"{label}: {basis[0]}\" if basis else label\n\n\n__all__ = [\"candidates\", \"card\", \"find_for_test\", \"find_for_text\",\n          \"import_mes_log\", \"list_mes_scans\", \"health_line\"]\n","numLines":246,"startLine":1,"totalLines":246}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bf4a48f4-8822-4f3c-90e9-b697a2fb5200","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"7bb2d4d6-00d4-4dfd-a6dc-64eda29d6ef5","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7f5dba9e9d416cc6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2QWJkS6g9oEhLetv2bB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018TnucTjZz2Y9SbxfqmXenL","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_mes_handoff.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9003,"cache_read_input_tokens":57019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9003,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018TnucTjZz2Y9SbxfqmXenL":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_mes_handoff.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"58723456-c990-452f-99b1-657b43873c16","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cg2QWJVYr7DziFqH7AZXp","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1da9b3f4-c8fb-4e18-8978-c45da3f3b602","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:58:47.160Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"1da9b3f4-c8fb-4e18-8978-c45da3f3b602","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4f6844c0-3b82-41b2-99e4-abe62041f502","agentId":"a7f5dba9e9d416cc6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018TnucTjZz2Y9SbxfqmXenL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Checks for the MES-vs-CUORE capability matrix, the knowledge table it is\n2\tgenerated from, the MES handoff cards (Tests page + job page step 6), and\n3\tMES-log import into a \"Scans, source MES\" entry with a health report.\n4\t\n5\tSame posture as ``cuore/tests/check_marque_port.py``: ``CUORE_STATE_DIR``\n6\tand ``MES_LOG_DIR`` are both pointed at throwaway directories BEFORE\n7\t``cuore`` (and therefore ``mes``) is imported, and a synthetic\n8\t``SCAN_2610080920.txt`` is written into that throwaway MES root -- this\n9\tcheck is fully self-contained and does not touch the real MultiEcuScan\n10\tinstall or the real Stelvio corpus.\n11\t\n12\tFive groups of checks:\n13\t  1. The knowledge table (``mes.mes_functions``) has at least 25 functions,\n14\t     every one with a non-empty ``source``, and no duplicate ids.\n15\t  2. ``cuore.services.mes_handoff_bridge.card``/``find_for_test`` renders a\n16\t     handoff card for ``esim_commanded_vent_test`` with its MES menu path\n17\t     and at least one prerequisite -- and never claims to write to the car\n18\t     (``writes_to_car`` is always ``False``).\n19\t  3. ``GET /api/tests/mes-handoff/candidates`` returns >=25 functions;\n20\t     ``GET /api/tests/mes-handoff/by-test/esim_commanded_vent_test`` returns\n21\t     that same card over HTTP.\n22\t  4. Recording a test result still round-trips (regression on the existing\n23\t     ``POST /api/tests/{vin}/{test_id}/result`` contract this feature sits\n24\t     beside, never replaces).\n25\t  5. Importing the synthetic ``SCAN_2610080920.txt`` (via the bridge\n26\t     directly, and again via ``POST /api/tests/{vin}/mes-import``) yields a\n27\t     \"Scans\" entry tagged ``source.kind == \"MES\"`` with a non-empty health\n28\t     report line, and ``GET /api/tests/{vin}/mes-scans`` lists it back; the\n29\t     Tests page and job page step 6 both render the handoff include marker.\n30\t\n31\tRun:\n32\t    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_mes_handoff.py\n33\t\"\"\"\n34\t\n35\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n36\t\n37\timport os\n38\timport sys\n39\timport tempfile\n40\tfrom pathlib import Path\n41\t\n42\tVIN = \"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\"  # the Stelvio -- same fixture VIN every other check uses\n43\t\n44\t_STATE_DIR = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-mes-handoff-state-\")\n45\t_MES_DIR = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-mes-handoff-logs-\"))\n46\t\n47\tos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = _STATE_DIR\n48\tos.environ[\"MES_LOG_DIR\"] = str(_MES_DIR)\n49\tos.environ.pop(\"CUORE_AUDIT_PATH\", None)\n50\tos.environ.pop(\"MES_LOG_DIRS\", None)\n51\t\n52\t_SCAN_NAME = \"SCAN_2610080920.txt\"\n53\t(_MES_DIR / _SCAN_NAME).write_text(\n54\t    \"Engine / ECM (Engine Control Module)\\n\"\n55\t    \"Bosch MED17 ECM\\n\"\n56\t    \"ISO Code: 01 02 03 04 05\\n\"\n57\t    f\"VIN code: {VIN}\\n\"\n58\t    \"Hardware number: 1234 - Ver: 01\\n\"\n59\t    \"Software number: 5678 - Ver: 01\\n\"\n60\t    \"Errors found:\\n\"\n61\t    \"P0455-00 - Evaporative Emission System Leak Detected (large leak)\\n\",\n62\t    encoding=\"utf-8\",\n63\t)\n64\t\n65\tROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\n66\tsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n67\t\n68\tfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient  # noqa: E402\n69\t\n70\tfrom cuore.app import create_app  # noqa: E402\n71\tfrom cuore.services import mes_handoff_bridge  # noqa: E402\n72\t\n73\tfrom mes import mes_functions  # noqa: E402\n74\t\n75\tfailures: list[str] = []\n76\tchecks = 0\n77\t\n78\t\n79\tdef check(label: str, cond: bool, detail: str = \"\") -> None:\n80\t    global checks\n81\t    checks += 1\n82\t    mark = \"ok\" if cond else \"FAIL\"\n83\t    print(f\"  [{mark}] {label}\" + (f\" -- {detail}\" if detail and not cond else \"\"))\n84\t    if not cond:\n85\t        failures.append(label)\n86\t\n87\t\n88\t# ===========================================================================\n89\t# 1. the knowledge table\n90\t# ===========================================================================\n91\t\n92\tprint(\"=== mes_functions knowledge table ===\")\n93\tfns = mes_functions.all_functions()\n94\tcheck(\"at least 25 MES functions catalogued\", len(fns) >= 25, str(len(fns)))\n95\tcheck(\"no duplicate ids\", len({f[\"id\"] for f in fns}) == len(fns))\n96\tno_source = [f[\"id\"] for f in fns if not (f.get(\"source\") or \"\").strip()]\n97\tcheck(\"every function has a non-empty source\", not no_source, str(no_source))\n98\tbad_kind = [f[\"id\"] for f in fns if f[\"kind\"] not in mes_functions.KINDS]\n99\tcheck(\"every function's kind is one of KINDS\", not bad_kind, str(bad_kind))\n100\tcheck(\"function() returns None for an unknown id\",\n101\t     mes_functions.function(\"not-a-real-id\") is None)\n102\tcheck(\"esim_commanded_vent_test is in the catalogue (cross-ref to \"\n103\t     \"mechanic_tests.py)\", mes_functions.function(\"esim_commanded_vent_test\")\n104\t     is not None)\n105\t\n106\t# ===========================================================================\n107\t# 2. handoff card rendering\n108\t# ===========================================================================\n109\t\n110\tprint(\"=== handoff card: esim_commanded_vent_test ===\")\n111\tcard = mes_handoff_bridge.find_for_test(\"esim_commanded_vent_test\")\n112\tcheck(\"a handoff card was found for esim_commanded_vent_test\", card is not None)\n113\tif card is not None:\n114\t    check(\"the card names the MES menu path\", \"Actuators\" in card[\"menu_path\"],\n115\t         card[\"menu_path\"])\n116\t    check(\"the card carries at least one prerequisite\",\n117\t         len(card[\"prerequisites\"]) >= 1, str(card[\"prerequisites\"]))\n118\t    check(\"the card never claims to write to the car\",\n119\t         card[\"writes_to_car\"] is False)\n120\t    check(\"the card names a source\", bool((card.get(\"source\") or \"\").strip()))\n121\t\n122\tcheck(\"find_for_test returns None for a test with no MES-only counterpart\",\n123\t     mes_handoff_bridge.find_for_test(\"not-a-real-test-id\") is None)\n124\tcheck(\"find_for_text matches a function by free-text name\",\n125\t     mes_handoff_bridge.find_for_text(\"Service interval reset\") is not None)\n126\t\n127\t# ===========================================================================\n128\t# 3. HTTP surface\n129\t# ===========================================================================\n130\t\n131\tprint(\"=== HTTP: /api/tests/mes-handoff/* ===\")\n132\tclient = TestClient(create_app())\n133\t\n134\tcands = client.get(\"/api/tests/mes-handoff/candidates\")\n135\tcheck(\"candidates responds 200\", cands.status_code == 200, str(cands.status_code))\n136\tcand_fns = cands.json().get(\"functions\", [])\n137\tcheck(\"candidates returns >=25 functions\", len(cand_fns) >= 25, str(len(cand_fns)))\n138\t\n139\tby_test = client.get(\"/api/tests/mes-handoff/by-test/esim_commanded_vent_test\")\n140\tcheck(\"by-test responds 200\", by_test.status_code == 200, str(by_test.status_code))\n141\tby_test_handoff = by_test.json().get(\"handoff\")\n142\tcheck(\"by-test returns a non-null handoff card\", by_test_handoff is not None)\n143\tif by_test_handoff is not None:\n144\t    check(\"by-test's card matches the bridge's own card id\",\n145\t         by_test_handoff[\"id\"] == \"esim_commanded_vent_test\", str(by_test_handoff))\n146\t\n147\tby_text = client.get(\"/api/tests/mes-handoff/by-text\", params={\"text\": \"service interval reset\"})\n148\tcheck(\"by-text responds 200\", by_text.status_code == 200, str(by_text.status_code))\n149\tcheck(\"by-text returns a non-null handoff card\", by_text.json().get(\"handoff\") is not None)\n150\t\n151\t# ===========================================================================\n152\t# 4. regression: recording a test result still works\n153\t# ===========================================================================\n154\t\n155\tprint(\"=== regression: POST /api/tests/{vin}/{test_id}/result ===\")\n156\tresult_resp = client.post(\n157\t    f\"/api/tests/{VIN}/esim_commanded_vent_test/result\",\n158\t    json={\"result\": \"inconclusive\", \"reason\": \"no wiTECH on hand this visit\"},\n159\t)\n160\tcheck(\"recording a result still responds 200\", result_resp.status_code == 200,\n161\t     str(result_resp.status_code))\n162\tcheck(\"the recorded result round-trips\",\n163\t     result_resp.json().get(\"result\") == \"inconclusive\", str(result_resp.json()))\n164\t\n165\ttests_page = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/tests\")\n166\tcheck(\"the Tests page still responds 200\", tests_page.status_code == 200,\n167\t     str(tests_page.status_code))\n168\tcheck(\"the Tests page wires in the MES handoff include\",\n169\t     'id=\"mes-handoff-root\"' in tests_page.text)\n170\t\n171\t# ===========================================================================\n172\t# 5. MES log import -> a Scans entry, source MES, with a health report\n173\t# ===========================================================================\n174\t\n175\tprint(\"=== MES log import ===\")\n176\tscan = mes_handoff_bridge.import_mes_log(VIN, _SCAN_NAME)\n177\tcheck(\"the imported scan is tagged source.kind == MES\",\n178\t     scan.get(\"source\", {}).get(\"kind\") == \"MES\", str(scan.get(\"source\")))\n179\tcheck(\"the imported scan carries the DTC the fixture log has\",\n180\t     \"P0455-00\" in scan[\"dtcs\"][\"stored\"], str(scan[\"dtcs\"]))\n181\tline = mes_handoff_bridge.health_line(scan)\n182\tcheck(\"a non-empty health report line was produced\", bool(line.strip()), repr(line))\n183\t\n184\tlisted = mes_handoff_bridge.list_mes_scans(VIN)\n185\tcheck(\"list_mes_scans shows the imported scan\",\n186\t     any(s[\"id\"] == scan[\"id\"] for s in listed), str(listed))\n187\t\n188\timport_resp = client.post(f\"/api/tests/{VIN}/mes-import\", json={\"name\": _SCAN_NAME})\n189\tcheck(\"POST mes-import responds 200\", import_resp.status_code == 200,\n190\t     str(import_resp.status_code))\n191\timport_body = import_resp.json()\n192\tcheck(\"the HTTP import also tags source.kind == MES\",\n193\t     import_body.get(\"scan\", {}).get(\"source\", {}).get(\"kind\") == \"MES\",\n194\t     str(import_body))\n195\tcheck(\"the HTTP import returns a non-empty health_line\",\n196\t     bool((import_body.get(\"health_line\") or \"\").strip()), str(import_body))\n197\t\n198\tscans_resp = client.get(f\"/api/tests/{VIN}/mes-scans\")\n199\tcheck(\"GET mes-scans responds 200\", scans_resp.status_code == 200,\n200\t     str(scans_resp.status_code))\n201\tscans_body = scans_resp.json()\n202\tcheck(\"mes-scans lists at least one scan with source MES\",\n203\t     any(s.get(\"source\", {}).get(\"kind\") == \"MES\" for s in scans_body.get(\"scans\", [])),\n204\t     str(scans_body))\n205\tcheck(\"mes-scans returns a parallel non-empty health line per scan\",\n206\t     len(scans_body.get(\"lines\", [])) == len(scans_body.get(\"scans\", []))\n207\t     and all((l or \"\").strip() for l in scans_body.get(\"lines\", [])),\n208\t     str(scans_body))\n209\t\n210\t# a VIN mismatch is rejected, not silently filed under the wrong car\n211\ttry:\n212\t    mes_handoff_bridge.import_mes_log(\"ZN661XUA9JX000001\", _SCAN_NAME)\n213\t    check(\"importing a log for the wrong VIN raises\", False)\n214\texcept Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001\n215\t    check(\"importing a log for the wrong VIN raises BadRequest\",\n216\t         \"VIN\" in str(exc), str(exc))\n217\t\n218\tprint(\"=== job page step 6 wires in the MES handoff include ===\")\n219\topen_resp = client.post(f\"/v/{VIN}/job/open\",\n220\t                        data={\"technician\": \"tester\", \"complaint\": \"CEL\"},\n221\t                        follow_redirects=True)\n222\tcheck(\"opening a case responds 200\", open_resp.status_code == 200,\n223\t     str(open_resp.status_code))\n224\tjob_step6 = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/job\", params={\"step\": \"6\"})\n225\tcheck(\"job page step 6 responds 200\", job_step6.status_code == 200,\n226\t     str(job_step6.status_code))\n227\tcheck(\"job page step 6 wires in the MES handoff include\",\n228\t     'id=\"mes-handoff-root\"' in job_step6.text)\n229\t\n230\t# ===========================================================================\n231\tprint(f\"\\n{checks} checks, {len(failures)} failures\")\n232\tif failures:\n233\t    for f in failures:\n234\t        print(f\"FAILED: {f}\")\n235\t    sys.exit(1)\n236\tprint(\"All checks passed.\")\n237\t"}]},"uuid":"2c928eea-1c2f-48f9-b7d8-945cd877b8dd","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:58:47.279Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_mes_handoff.py","content":"\"\"\"Checks for the MES-vs-CUORE capability matrix, the knowledge table it is\ngenerated from, the MES handoff cards (Tests page + job page step 6), and\nMES-log import into a \"Scans, source MES\" entry with a health report.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore/tests/check_marque_port.py``: ``CUORE_STATE_DIR``\nand ``MES_LOG_DIR`` are both pointed at throwaway directories BEFORE\n``cuore`` (and therefore ``mes``) is imported, and a synthetic\n``SCAN_2610080920.txt`` is written into that throwaway MES root -- this\ncheck is fully self-contained and does not touch the real MultiEcuScan\ninstall or the real Stelvio corpus.\n\nFive groups of checks:\n  1. The knowledge table (``mes.mes_functions``) has at least 25 functions,\n     every one with a non-empty ``source``, and no duplicate ids.\n  2. ``cuore.services.mes_handoff_bridge.card``/``find_for_test`` renders a\n     handoff card for ``esim_commanded_vent_test`` with its MES menu path\n     and at least one prerequisite -- and never claims to write to the car\n     (``writes_to_car`` is always ``False``).\n  3. ``GET /api/tests/mes-handoff/candidates`` returns >=25 functions;\n     ``GET /api/tests/mes-handoff/by-test/esim_commanded_vent_test`` returns\n     that same card over HTTP.\n  4. Recording a test result still round-trips (regression on the existing\n     ``POST /api/tests/{vin}/{test_id}/result`` contract this feature sits\n     beside, never replaces).\n  5. Importing the synthetic ``SCAN_2610080920.txt`` (via the bridge\n     directly, and again via ``POST /api/tests/{vin}/mes-import``) yields a\n     \"Scans\" entry tagged ``source.kind == \"MES\"`` with a non-empty health\n     report line, and ``GET /api/tests/{vin}/mes-scans`` lists it back; the\n     Tests page and job page step 6 both render the handoff include marker.\n\nRun:\n    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_mes_handoff.py\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nVIN = \"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\"  # the Stelvio -- same fixture VIN every other check uses\n\n_STATE_DIR = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-mes-handoff-state-\")\n_MES_DIR = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-mes-handoff-logs-\"))\n\nos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = _STATE_DIR\nos.environ[\"MES_LOG_DIR\"] = str(_MES_DIR)\nos.environ.pop(\"CUORE_AUDIT_PATH\", None)\nos.environ.pop(\"MES_LOG_DIRS\", None)\n\n_SCAN_NAME = \"SCAN_2610080920.txt\"\n(_MES_DIR / _SCAN_NAME).write_text(\n    \"Engine / ECM (Engine Control Module)\\n\"\n    \"Bosch MED17 ECM\\n\"\n    \"ISO Code: 01 02 03 04 05\\n\"\n    f\"VIN code: {VIN}\\n\"\n    \"Hardware number: 1234 - Ver: 01\\n\"\n    \"Software number: 5678 - Ver: 01\\n\"\n    \"Errors found:\\n\"\n    \"P0455-00 - Evaporative Emission System Leak Detected (large leak)\\n\",\n    encoding=\"utf-8\",\n)\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nsys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom cuore.app import create_app  # noqa: E402\nfrom cuore.services import mes_handoff_bridge  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom mes import mes_functions  # noqa: E402\n\nfailures: list[str] = []\nchecks = 0\n\n\ndef check(label: str, cond: bool, detail: str = \"\") -> None:\n    global checks\n    checks += 1\n    mark = \"ok\" if cond else \"FAIL\"\n    print(f\"  [{mark}] {label}\" + (f\" -- {detail}\" if detail and not cond else \"\"))\n    if not cond:\n        failures.append(label)\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 1. the knowledge table\n# ===========================================================================\n\nprint(\"=== mes_functions knowledge table ===\")\nfns = mes_functions.all_functions()\ncheck(\"at least 25 MES functions catalogued\", len(fns) >= 25, str(len(fns)))\ncheck(\"no duplicate ids\", len({f[\"id\"] for f in fns}) == len(fns))\nno_source = [f[\"id\"] for f in fns if not (f.get(\"source\") or \"\").strip()]\ncheck(\"every function has a non-empty source\", not no_source, str(no_source))\nbad_kind = [f[\"id\"] for f in fns if f[\"kind\"] not in mes_functions.KINDS]\ncheck(\"every function's kind is one of KINDS\", not bad_kind, str(bad_kind))\ncheck(\"function() returns None for an unknown id\",\n     mes_functions.function(\"not-a-real-id\") is None)\ncheck(\"esim_commanded_vent_test is in the catalogue (cross-ref to \"\n     \"mechanic_tests.py)\", mes_functions.function(\"esim_commanded_vent_test\")\n     is not None)\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 2. handoff card rendering\n# ===========================================================================\n\nprint(\"=== handoff card: esim_commanded_vent_test ===\")\ncard = mes_handoff_bridge.find_for_test(\"esim_commanded_vent_test\")\ncheck(\"a handoff card was found for esim_commanded_vent_test\", card is not None)\nif card is not None:\n    check(\"the card names the MES menu path\", \"Actuators\" in card[\"menu_path\"],\n         card[\"menu_path\"])\n    check(\"the card carries at least one prerequisite\",\n         len(card[\"prerequisites\"]) >= 1, str(card[\"prerequisites\"]))\n    check(\"the card never claims to write to the car\",\n         card[\"writes_to_car\"] is False)\n    check(\"the card names a source\", bool((card.get(\"source\") or \"\").strip()))\n\ncheck(\"find_for_test returns None for a test with no MES-only counterpart\",\n     mes_handoff_bridge.find_for_test(\"not-a-real-test-id\") is None)\ncheck(\"find_for_text matches a function by free-text name\",\n     mes_handoff_bridge.find_for_text(\"Service interval reset\") is not None)\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 3. HTTP surface\n# ===========================================================================\n\nprint(\"=== HTTP: /api/tests/mes-handoff/* ===\")\nclient = TestClient(create_app())\n\ncands = client.get(\"/api/tests/mes-handoff/candidates\")\ncheck(\"candidates responds 200\", cands.status_code == 200, str(cands.status_code))\ncand_fns = cands.json().get(\"functions\", [])\ncheck(\"candidates returns >=25 functions\", len(cand_fns) >= 25, str(len(cand_fns)))\n\nby_test = client.get(\"/api/tests/mes-handoff/by-test/esim_commanded_vent_test\")\ncheck(\"by-test responds 200\", by_test.status_code == 200, str(by_test.status_code))\nby_test_handoff = by_test.json().get(\"handoff\")\ncheck(\"by-test returns a non-null handoff card\", by_test_handoff is not None)\nif by_test_handoff is not None:\n    check(\"by-test's card matches the bridge's own card id\",\n         by_test_handoff[\"id\"] == \"esim_commanded_vent_test\", str(by_test_handoff))\n\nby_text = client.get(\"/api/tests/mes-handoff/by-text\", params={\"text\": \"service interval reset\"})\ncheck(\"by-text responds 200\", by_text.status_code == 200, str(by_text.status_code))\ncheck(\"by-text returns a non-null handoff card\", by_text.json().get(\"handoff\") is not None)\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 4. regression: recording a test result still works\n# ===========================================================================\n\nprint(\"=== regression: POST /api/tests/{vin}/{test_id}/result ===\")\nresult_resp = client.post(\n    f\"/api/tests/{VIN}/esim_commanded_vent_test/result\",\n    json={\"result\": \"inconclusive\", \"reason\": \"no wiTECH on hand this visit\"},\n)\ncheck(\"recording a result still responds 200\", result_resp.status_code == 200,\n     str(result_resp.status_code))\ncheck(\"the recorded result round-trips\",\n     result_resp.json().get(\"result\") == \"inconclusive\", str(result_resp.json()))\n\ntests_page = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/tests\")\ncheck(\"the Tests page still responds 200\", tests_page.status_code == 200,\n     str(tests_page.status_code))\ncheck(\"the Tests page wires in the MES handoff include\",\n     'id=\"mes-handoff-root\"' in tests_page.text)\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# 5. MES log import -> a Scans entry, source MES, with a health report\n# ===========================================================================\n\nprint(\"=== MES log import ===\")\nscan = mes_handoff_bridge.import_mes_log(VIN, _SCAN_NAME)\ncheck(\"the imported scan is tagged source.kind == MES\",\n     scan.get(\"source\", {}).get(\"kind\") == \"MES\", str(scan.get(\"source\")))\ncheck(\"the imported scan carries the DTC the fixture log has\",\n     \"P0455-00\" in scan[\"dtcs\"][\"stored\"], str(scan[\"dtcs\"]))\nline = mes_handoff_bridge.health_line(scan)\ncheck(\"a non-empty health report line was produced\", bool(line.strip()), repr(line))\n\nlisted = mes_handoff_bridge.list_mes_scans(VIN)\ncheck(\"list_mes_scans shows the imported scan\",\n     any(s[\"id\"] == scan[\"id\"] for s in listed), str(listed))\n\nimport_resp = client.post(f\"/api/tests/{VIN}/mes-import\", json={\"name\": _SCAN_NAME})\ncheck(\"POST mes-import responds 200\", import_resp.status_code == 200,\n     str(import_resp.status_code))\nimport_body = import_resp.json()\ncheck(\"the HTTP import also tags source.kind == MES\",\n     import_body.get(\"scan\", {}).get(\"source\", {}).get(\"kind\") == \"MES\",\n     str(import_body))\ncheck(\"the HTTP import returns a non-empty health_line\",\n     bool((import_body.get(\"health_line\") or \"\").strip()), str(import_body))\n\nscans_resp = client.get(f\"/api/tests/{VIN}/mes-scans\")\ncheck(\"GET mes-scans responds 200\", scans_resp.status_code == 200,\n     str(scans_resp.status_code))\nscans_body = scans_resp.json()\ncheck(\"mes-scans lists at least one scan with source MES\",\n     any(s.get(\"source\", {}).get(\"kind\") == \"MES\" for s in scans_body.get(\"scans\", [])),\n     str(scans_body))\ncheck(\"mes-scans returns a parallel non-empty health line per scan\",\n     len(scans_body.get(\"lines\", [])) == len(scans_body.get(\"scans\", []))\n     and all((l or \"\").strip() for l in scans_body.get(\"lines\", [])),\n     str(scans_body))\n\n# a VIN mismatch is rejected, not silently filed under the wrong car\ntry:\n    mes_handoff_bridge.import_mes_log(\"ZN661XUA9JX000001\", _SCAN_NAME)\n    check(\"importing a log for the wrong VIN raises\", False)\nexcept Exception as exc:  # noqa: BLE001\n    check(\"importing a log for the wrong VIN raises BadRequest\",\n         \"VIN\" in str(exc), str(exc))\n\nprint(\"=== job page step 6 wires in the MES handoff include ===\")\nopen_resp = client.post(f\"/v/{VIN}/job/open\",\n                        data={\"technician\": \"tester\", \"complaint\": \"CEL\"},\n                        follow_redirects=True)\ncheck(\"opening a case responds 200\", open_resp.status_code == 200,\n     str(open_resp.status_code))\njob_step6 = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/job\", params={\"step\": \"6\"})\ncheck(\"job page step 6 responds 200\", job_step6.status_code == 200,\n     str(job_step6.status_code))\ncheck(\"job page step 6 wires in the MES handoff include\",\n     'id=\"mes-handoff-root\"' in job_step6.text)\n\n# ===========================================================================\nprint(f\"\\n{checks} checks, {len(failures)} failures\")\nif failures:\n    for f in failures:\n        print(f\"FAILED: {f}\")\n    sys.exit(1)\nprint(\"All checks passed.\")\n","numLines":237,"startLine":1,"totalLines":237}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1da9b3f4-c8fb-4e18-8978-c45da3f3b602","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"2c928eea-1c2f-48f9-b7d8-945cd877b8dd","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7f5dba9e9d416cc6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2QWJkS6g9oEhLetv2bB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017i1CiJ3yp4hAqJ99hNV1vJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_scanlog.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9003,"cache_read_input_tokens":57019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9003,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017i1CiJ3yp4hAqJ99hNV1vJ":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_scanlog.py"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"58723456-c990-452f-99b1-657b43873c16","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011Cg2QWJVYr7DziFqH7AZXp","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8135d8bd-ee29-4729-832b-43e119999e83","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:58:47.575Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"8135d8bd-ee29-4729-832b-43e119999e83","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4f6844c0-3b82-41b2-99e4-abe62041f502","agentId":"a7f5dba9e9d416cc6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017i1CiJ3yp4hAqJ99hNV1vJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Checks for the scan log (``cuore.live.scanlog``, ``cuore.services.scanlog_bridge``,\n2\t``cuore.api.scanlog``, ``cuore.web.scanlog_routes``).\n3\t\n4\tAnswers the owner's question \"does CUORE have a log area to save the freeze\n5\tframe data?\" -- it did not; this groups the from-car rows already appended\n6\tto ``observations.jsonl`` into browsable scans on read. Nothing here is a\n7\tsecond copy of the truth and nothing here opens COM3 or calls a live\n8\tadapter endpoint: every observation below is a hand-built fixture appended\n9\tstraight to a throwaway ``observations.jsonl`` (same posture as\n10\t``cuore/tests/check_detail.py``/``check_dossier_view.py``), tagged with a\n11\treal ``stream=\"serial COM3@115200\"`` value so ``is_from_car`` accepts it the\n12\tsame way a real bench read would.\n13\t\n14\tSame posture as ``cuore/tests/check_dossier_view.py``: ``CUORE_STATE_DIR``\n15\tpoints at a throwaway directory BEFORE cuore is imported, and this app's own\n16\trouter may not be wired into ``create_app()`` yet elsewhere in a concurrent\n17\tedit -- it is included defensively if missing.\n18\t\n19\tRun:\n20\t    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_scanlog.py\n21\t    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_screens.py\n22\t\"\"\"\n23\t\n24\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n25\t\n26\timport json\n27\timport os\n28\timport sys\n29\timport tempfile\n30\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n31\tfrom pathlib import Path\n32\t\n33\tos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-scanlog-\")\n34\tos.environ.pop(\"CUORE_AUDIT_PATH\", None)\n35\t\n36\tsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]))\n37\t\n38\tfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient  # noqa: E402\n39\t\n40\tfrom cuore.app import create_app  # noqa: E402\n41\tfrom cuore.api import scanlog as scanlog_api  # noqa: E402\n42\tfrom cuore.web import scanlog_routes  # noqa: E402\n43\tfrom cuore.live import scanlog, store as live_store  # noqa: E402\n44\tfrom cuore.services import scanlog_bridge  # noqa: E402\n45\tfrom cuore.services.errors import NotFound  # noqa: E402\n46\t\n47\tVIN = \"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\"  # the Stelvio -- real VIN used across this suite's fixtures\n48\t\n49\tfailures: list[str] = []\n50\tchecks = 0\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tdef check(label: str, cond: bool, detail: str = \"\") -> None:\n54\t    global checks\n55\t    checks += 1\n56\t    mark = \"ok\" if cond else \"FAIL\"\n57\t    print(f\"  [{mark}] {label}\" + (f\" -- {detail}\" if detail and not cond else \"\"))\n58\t    if not cond:\n59\t        failures.append(label)\n60\t\n61\t\n62\tapp = create_app()\n63\texisting_paths = {getattr(r, \"path\", None) for r in app.routes}\n64\tif \"/api/scans/{vin}\" not in existing_paths:\n65\t    app.include_router(scanlog_api.router, prefix=\"/api\")\n66\tif \"/v/{vin}/scans\" not in existing_paths:\n67\t    app.include_router(scanlog_routes.router)\n68\tclient = TestClient(app)\n69\t\n70\t\n71\tdef _write(at: datetime, kind: str, data: dict, *, vin: str = \"\",\n72\t          stream: str = \"serial COM3@115200\") -> None:\n73\t    entry = {\"at\": at.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"), \"kind\": kind, \"vin\": vin,\n74\t             \"bus\": \"can_c\", \"cable\": \"none\", \"stream\": stream, \"data\": data}\n75\t    with live_store.observations_path().open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n76\t        f.write(json.dumps(entry) + \"\\n\")\n77\t\n78\t\n79\t# ===========================================================================\n80\t# Fixture: one older, clean scan; one newer scan with findings; one\n81\t# demo/replay row that must never surface as a scan of its own.\n82\t# ===========================================================================\n83\t\n84\tOLDER = datetime(2026, 10, 13, 18, 0, 0)\n85\t_write(OLDER, \"obd_dtcs\", {\"kind\": \"stored\", \"dtcs\": [], \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": []}})\n86\t_write(OLDER + timedelta(minutes=1), \"readiness\",\n87\t      {\"since_clear\": {\"mil_on\": False, \"stored_dtc_count\": 0,\n88\t                        \"monitors\": [{\"monitor\": \"Evaporative system\", \"supported\": True,\n89\t                                      \"complete\": True}],\n90\t                        \"all_complete\": True}}, vin=VIN)\n91\t# A full/guided scan's own scan_coverage observation, same cluster (within\n92\t# WINDOW of the readiness read above): CAN-C swept (5 modules answered),\n93\t# IHS/CH never attempted -- the exact coverage line the owner's own spec\n94\t# quotes.\n95\t_write(OLDER + timedelta(minutes=2), \"scan_coverage\", {\n96\t    \"scan_id\": \"SCAN_\" + OLDER.strftime(\"%y%m%d%H%M\"), \"vin\": VIN, \"cable\": \"none\",\n97\t    \"buses_attempted\": [\"can_c\"], \"duration_s\": 12.0, \"steps\": [],\n98\t    \"coverage\": [{\"bus\": \"can_c\", \"module\": m, \"category\": \"answered\", \"why\": None,\n99\t                  \"active\": 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0}\n100\t                for m in (\"ECM\", \"IPC\", \"TCM\", \"DTCM\", \"ESM\")],\n101\t    \"counts\": {\"active\": 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0},\n102\t}, vin=VIN)\n103\t\n104\t# A demo/replay read, timestamped well clear of either real window (>15 min\n105\t# from both), tagged with a non-serial stream -- is_from_car() must reject\n106\t# it outright, so it must never become a scan, and P9999 must never appear\n107\t# anywhere in the scan log.\n108\t_write(OLDER + timedelta(hours=1), \"obd_dtcs\", {\"kind\": \"stored\", \"dtcs\": [\"P9999\"]},\n109\t      vin=VIN, stream=\"demo\")\n110\t\n111\t# A manual, single-purpose read (Codes/Live/Tests, not a guided/full scan)\n112\t# more than 15 min clear of both real windows -- its own \"partial\" scan:\n113\t# still a scan (counted by scan_plan), but with no scan_coverage observation\n114\t# at all.\n115\tPARTIAL = OLDER + timedelta(minutes=40)\n116\t_write(PARTIAL, \"freeze_frame\",\n117\t      {\"pid\": \"02\", \"name\": None, \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": {\"dtc\": \"P0128\", \"bytes\": [\"00\", \"00\"]}}},\n118\t      vin=VIN)\n119\tPARTIAL_ID = PARTIAL.strftime(scanlog.ID_FMT)\n120\t\n121\tNEWER = datetime(2026, 10, 13, 20, 0, 0)\n122\t_write(NEWER, \"obd_dtcs\",\n123\t      {\"kind\": \"stored\", \"dtcs\": [\"P0440\"], \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": [\"P0440\"]}})\n124\t_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=3), \"obd_dtcs\",\n125\t      {\"kind\": \"pending\", \"dtcs\": [\"P0455\"], \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": [\"P0455\"]}})\n126\t_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=6), \"readiness\",\n127\t      {\"since_clear\": {\"mil_on\": True, \"stored_dtc_count\": 1,\n128\t                        \"monitors\": [{\"monitor\": \"Evaporative system\", \"supported\": True,\n129\t                                      \"complete\": True}],\n130\t                        \"all_complete\": True}}, vin=VIN)\n131\t_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=9), \"mode06\",\n132\t      {\"results\": {\"3A\": {\"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": [\n133\t          {\"mid\": \"3A\", \"mid_name\": \"EVAP leak monitor\", \"tid\": \"91\", \"uasid\": \"30\",\n134\t           \"unit\": \"ms\", \"value\": 100, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 50, \"passed\": False}]}}},\n135\t       \"evap_summary\": [\"EVAP leak monitor: value 100 ms vs limit 50 ms -> FAIL\"]}, vin=VIN)\n136\t_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=12), \"freeze_frame\",\n137\t      {\"pid\": \"02\", \"name\": None, \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": {\"dtc\": \"P0440\", \"bytes\": [\"00\", \"00\"]}}})\n138\t_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=13), \"freeze_frame\",\n139\t      {\"pid\": \"2F\", \"name\": \"fuel_level\",\n140\t       \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": {\"pid\": \"2F\", \"name\": \"fuel_level\", \"bytes\": [\"6B\"],\n141\t                                \"unit\": \"%\", \"value\": 42.0}}})\n142\t# A guided scan: CAN-C (6 modules, one ACTIVE) and CAN-IHS (2 modules) swept,\n143\t# CAN-CH never attempted.\n144\t_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=14), \"scan_coverage\", {\n145\t    \"scan_id\": \"SCAN_\" + NEWER.strftime(\"%y%m%d%H%M\"), \"vin\": VIN, \"cable\": \"blue_a5\",\n146\t    \"buses_attempted\": [\"can_c\", \"can_ihs\"], \"duration_s\": 40.0, \"steps\": [],\n147\t    \"coverage\": ([{\"bus\": \"can_c\", \"module\": m, \"category\": \"answered\", \"why\": None,\n148\t                  \"active\": 1 if m == \"ECM\" else 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0}\n149\t                 for m in (\"ECM\", \"IPC\", \"TCM\", \"DTCM\", \"ESM\", \"BCM\")]\n150\t                + [{\"bus\": \"can_ihs\", \"module\": m, \"category\": \"answered\", \"why\": None,\n151\t                   \"active\": 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0}\n152\t                  for m in (\"RFHUB\", \"DASM\")]),\n153\t    \"counts\": {\"active\": 1, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0},\n154\t    \"guided\": True, \"guided_status\": \"done\",\n155\t}, vin=VIN)\n156\t\n157\tNEWER_ID = NEWER.strftime(scanlog.ID_FMT)\n158\tOLDER_ID = OLDER.strftime(scanlog.ID_FMT)\n159\t\n160\t# A failed full-scan attempt (2026-10-14 honesty fix): a scan_coverage\n161\t# observation exists -- this WAS a fullscan/guided attempt, not a manual\n162\t# read -- but every row is \"not_reachable\" (adapter/cable error, e.g.\n163\t# COM3 failing to open): no module answered on any bus. Placed well\n164\t# before OLDER so it stays the OLDEST scan and never disturbs \"newest\"\n165\t# (NEWER_ID) in the checks below.\n166\tATTEMPT = OLDER - timedelta(hours=2)\n167\t_write(ATTEMPT, \"scan_coverage\", {\n168\t    \"scan_id\": \"SCAN_\" + ATTEMPT.strftime(\"%y%m%d%H%M\"), \"vin\": VIN, \"cable\": \"none\",\n169\t    \"buses_attempted\": [\"can_c\"], \"duration_s\": 1.0, \"steps\": [],\n170\t    \"coverage\": [{\"bus\": \"can_c\", \"module\": m, \"category\": \"not_reachable\",\n171\t                 \"why\": \"LinkUnavailable: could not open COM3\", \"active\": 0,\n172\t                 \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0}\n173\t                for m in (\"ECM\", \"IPC\", \"TCM\", \"DTCM\", \"ESM\")],\n174\t    \"counts\": {\"active\": 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0},\n175\t}, vin=VIN)\n176\tATTEMPT_ID = ATTEMPT.strftime(scanlog.ID_FMT)\n177\t\n178\t\n179\t# ===========================================================================\n180\t# cuore.live.scanlog -- direct\n181\t# ===========================================================================\n182\t\n183\tscans = scanlog.list_scans(VIN)\n184\tcheck(\"exactly 4 scans are grouped for this VIN (attempt, older, partial, newer)\",\n185\t      len(scans) == 4, str(len(scans)))\n186\tcheck(\"newest scan listed first\", bool(scans) and scans[0][\"id\"] == NEWER_ID,\n187\t      str([s[\"id\"] for s in scans]))\n188\tcheck(\"no scan carries the demo-stream P9999 code\",\n189\t      not any(\"P9999\" in s[\"dtcs\"][\"stored\"] for s in scans), str(scans))\n190\t\n191\tnewest = scanlog.get_scan(VIN, NEWER_ID)\n192\tcheck(\"newest scan found by id\", newest is not None)\n193\tif newest:\n194\t    check(\"newest scan has stored P0440\", newest[\"dtcs\"][\"stored\"] == [\"P0440\"],\n195\t          str(newest[\"dtcs\"]))\n196\t    check(\"newest scan has pending P0455\", newest[\"dtcs\"][\"pending\"] == [\"P0455\"],\n197\t          str(newest[\"dtcs\"]))\n198\t    check(\"MIL is on\", newest[\"mil\"] is True, str(newest[\"mil\"]))\n199\t\n200\t    mode06_3a = next((r for r in newest[\"mode06\"] if r[\"mid\"] == \"3A\"), None)\n201\t    check(\"Mode 06 3A is present\", mode06_3a is not None, str(newest[\"mode06\"]))\n202\t    check(\"Mode 06 3A FAILed\", bool(mode06_3a) and mode06_3a[\"passed\"] is False,\n203\t          str(mode06_3a))\n204\t\n205\t    ff = next((f for f in newest[\"freeze_frames\"] if f[\"code\"] == \"P0440\"), None)\n206\t    check(\"a P0440 freeze frame is present\", ff is not None, str(newest[\"freeze_frames\"]))\n207\t    fuel = next((p for p in (ff or {}).get(\"pids\", []) if p[\"pid\"] == \"2F\"), None)\n208\t    check(\"the freeze frame lists the fuel_level PID\", fuel is not None, str(ff))\n209\t    check(\"its name is sentence-cased\", bool(fuel) and fuel[\"name\"] == \"Fuel level\",\n210\t          str(fuel))\n211\t    check(\"its value round-trips\", bool(fuel) and fuel[\"value\"] == 42.0, str(fuel))\n212\t\n213\tolder = scanlog.get_scan(VIN, OLDER_ID)\n214\tcheck(\"older scan found by id\", older is not None)\n215\tif older:\n216\t    check(\"older scan has no stored codes\", older[\"dtcs\"][\"stored\"] == [], str(older[\"dtcs\"]))\n217\t    check(\"older scan is not partial (it has a scan_coverage observation)\",\n218\t          older[\"partial\"] is False, str(older[\"partial\"]))\n219\t    check(\"older scan's status is 'complete' (CAN-C answered modules)\",\n220\t          older[\"status\"] == \"complete\", str(older[\"status\"]))\n221\t    check(\"older scan's coverage line matches the owner's own spec wording\",\n222\t          older[\"coverage\"][\"line\"] ==\n223\t          \"CAN-C 5 modules · IHS not scanned (blue A5) · CH not scanned (grey A6)\",\n224\t          str((older.get(\"coverage\") or {}).get(\"line\")))\n225\t\n226\tcheck(\"newest scan's coverage shows the IHS pass (guided scan)\",\n227\t      bool(newest) and \"IHS 2 modules\" in (newest[\"coverage\"] or {}).get(\"line\", \"\"),\n228\t      str((newest or {}).get(\"coverage\")))\n229\tcheck(\"newest scan is not partial\", bool(newest) and newest[\"partial\"] is False)\n230\tcheck(\"newest scan's status is 'complete'\", bool(newest) and newest[\"status\"] == \"complete\",\n231\t      str((newest or {}).get(\"status\")))\n232\t\n233\tpartial = scanlog.get_scan(VIN, PARTIAL_ID)\n234\tcheck(\"the manual freeze-panel-only scan is found by id\", partial is not None)\n235\tif partial:\n236\t    check(\"it has no scan_coverage observation -> coverage is None\",\n237\t          partial[\"coverage\"] is None, str(partial[\"coverage\"]))\n238\t    check(\"it is labelled partial\", partial[\"partial\"] is True, str(partial[\"partial\"]))\n239\t    check(\"its status is 'partial', not 'attempt' (never ran a bus sweep at all)\",\n240\t          partial[\"status\"] == \"partial\", str(partial[\"status\"]))\n241\t\n242\tattempt = scanlog.get_scan(VIN, ATTEMPT_ID)\n243\tcheck(\"the failed full-scan attempt is found by id\", attempt is not None)\n244\tif attempt:\n245\t    check(\"it has a scan_coverage observation (it WAS a bus-sweep attempt)\",\n246\t          attempt[\"coverage\"] is not None, str(attempt[\"coverage\"]))\n247\t    check(\"its status is 'attempt' (no module answered on any bus)\",\n248\t          attempt[\"status\"] == \"attempt\", str(attempt[\"status\"]))\n249\t    check(\"it is still marked partial for display purposes (not a complete scan)\",\n250\t          attempt[\"partial\"] is True, str(attempt[\"partial\"]))\n251\t\n252\tcheck(\"unknown scan id resolves to None\", scanlog.get_scan(VIN, \"SCAN_0000000000\") is None)\n253\tcheck(\"a different VIN sees no scans\", scanlog.list_scans(\"UNKNOWNVIN0000000\") == [])\n254\t\n255\t\n256\t# --- scan plan (the \"Scan n of 10\" chip) --------------------------------------\n257\t# 2026-10-14 honesty fix: only a COMPLETE scan counts -- the manual partial\n258\t# read and the failed COM3 attempt do not, so of the 4 scans on file only\n259\t# OLDER and NEWER (both complete) count toward \"Scan n of 10\".\n260\t\n261\tplan = scanlog.scan_plan(VIN)\n262\tcheck(\"scan_plan counts only COMPLETE scans (2 of 4 -- the manual partial \"\n263\t      \"read and the failed attempt don't count)\",\n264\t      plan == {\"count\": 2, \"total\": 10}, str(plan))\n265\tcheck(\"a vehicle with no scans plans 0 of 10\",\n266\t      scanlog.scan_plan(\"UNKNOWNVIN0000000\") == {\"count\": 0, \"total\": 10})\n267\t\n268\t\n269\t# --- diff --------------------------------------------------------------------\n270\t\n271\td = scanlog.diff(VIN, OLDER_ID, NEWER_ID)\n272\tcheck(\"diff between the two scans exists\", d is not None)\n273\tif d:\n274\t    check(\"diff reports P0440 added (stored)\", d[\"codes\"][\"stored\"][\"added\"] == [\"P0440\"],\n275\t          str(d[\"codes\"]))\n276\t    check(\"diff reports a Mode 06 3A change\", any(c[\"mid\"] == \"3A\" for c in d[\"mode06_changes\"]),\n277\t          str(d[\"mode06_changes\"]))\n278\t    check(\"diff reports a readiness/MIL change\",\n279\t          any(c[\"monitor\"] == \"MIL\" for c in d[\"readiness_changes\"]),\n280\t          str(d[\"readiness_changes\"]))\n281\t    check(\"diff reports the coverage change (IHS now swept)\",\n282\t          bool(d[\"coverage_changes\"]) and \"IHS 2 modules\" in d[\"coverage_changes\"][0][\"after\"],\n283\t          str(d[\"coverage_changes\"]))\n284\t    check(\"diff reports no status_changes between these two (no code moved bucket)\",\n285\t          d[\"status_changes\"] == [], str(d[\"status_changes\"]))\n286\tcheck(\"diff against an unknown scan id returns None\", scanlog.diff(VIN, OLDER_ID, \"SCAN_x\") is None)\n287\t\n288\t\n289\t# --- MES export ----------------------------------------------------------------\n290\t\n291\tmes_text = scanlog.export_mes_text(newest)\n292\t# cuore.bootstrap (imported as a side effect of cuore.app, above) already put\n293\t# mes-log-mcp's own \"mes\" package on sys.path -- the one place that happens,\n294\t# per that module's own docstring.\n295\tfrom mes import scan as mes_scan  # noqa: E402\n296\t\n297\tparsed = mes_scan.parse_scan_text(mes_text, name=f\"{NEWER_ID}.txt\")\n298\tall_codes = {d.code for d in parsed.all_dtcs}\n299\tcheck(\"the MES export parses\", parsed is not None)\n300\tcheck(\"the MES export's codes include P0440\", \"P0440\" in all_codes, str(all_codes))\n301\tcheck(\"the MES export's codes include P0455\", \"P0455\" in all_codes, str(all_codes))\n302\t\n303\twritten = scanlog.write_mes_export(VIN, NEWER_ID)\n304\tcheck(\"write_mes_export wrote under CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans/<vin>/, never MES's own folder\",\n305\t      written is not None and \"scans\" in written.parts and VIN in written.parts,\n306\t      str(written))\n307\t\n308\t\n309\t# ===========================================================================\n310\t# cuore.services.scanlog_bridge\n311\t# ===========================================================================\n312\t\n313\ttry:\n314\t    scanlog_bridge.scan(VIN, \"SCAN_0000000000\")\n315\t    check(\"bridge raises NotFound for an unknown scan id\", False)\n316\texcept NotFound:\n317\t    check(\"bridge raises NotFound for an unknown scan id\", True)\n318\t\n319\texport_json = scanlog_bridge.export(VIN, NEWER_ID, \"json\")\n320\tcheck(\"bridge json export carries the scan's own id\",\n321\t      export_json[\"content\"][\"id\"] == NEWER_ID, str(export_json[\"content\"].get(\"id\")))\n322\texport_mes = scanlog_bridge.export(VIN, NEWER_ID, \"mes\")\n323\tcheck(\"bridge mes export is text containing the stored code\",\n324\t      \"P0440\" in export_mes[\"content\"], export_mes[\"content\"][:200])\n325\t\n326\tcheck(\"bridge scan_plan matches cuore.live.scanlog.scan_plan\",\n327\t      scanlog_bridge.scan_plan(VIN) == {\"count\": 2, \"total\": 10},\n328\t      str(scanlog_bridge.scan_plan(VIN)))\n329\t\n330\t\n331\t# ===========================================================================\n332\t# HTTP: TestClient only, never COM3 / a live adapter endpoint\n333\t# ===========================================================================\n334\t\n335\tr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}\")\n336\tcheck(\"GET /api/scans/{vin} is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\n337\tcheck(\"it lists all 4 scans\", len(r.json()[\"scans\"]) == 4, str(r.json()))\n338\t\n339\tr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/{NEWER_ID}\")\n340\tcheck(\"GET /api/scans/{vin}/{id} is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\n341\t\n342\tr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/diff\", params={\"a\": OLDER_ID, \"b\": NEWER_ID})\n343\tcheck(\"GET /api/scans/{vin}/diff is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\n344\tcheck(\"it reports P0440 added\", r.json()[\"codes\"][\"stored\"][\"added\"] == [\"P0440\"], str(r.json()))\n345\t\n346\tr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/{NEWER_ID}/export\", params={\"fmt\": \"json\"})\n347\tcheck(\"export?fmt=json is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\n348\tr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/{NEWER_ID}/export\", params={\"fmt\": \"mes\"})\n349\tcheck(\"export?fmt=mes is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\n350\tcheck(\"the mes export body round-trips through the real parser\",\n351\t      \"P0440\" in {d.code for d in mes_scan.parse_scan_text(r.text).all_dtcs}, r.text[:200])\n352\t\n353\tr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/SCAN_0000000000\")\n354\tcheck(\"GET of an unknown scan is 404\", r.status_code == 404, str(r.status_code))\n355\t\n356\tr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans\")\n357\tcheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans page is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\n358\tcheck(\"the list page shows the newest scan's stored code\",\n359\t      \"P0440\" in r.text, \"P0440 not in page body\")\n360\tcheck(\"the list page shows the scan plan chip (2 complete scans on file, out of 10)\",\n361\t      \"Scan 2 of 10\" in r.text, \"'Scan 2 of 10' not in page body\")\n362\tcheck(\"the list page marks the manual scan partial\",\n363\t      \"partial\" in r.text, \"'partial' not in page body\")\n364\tcheck(\"the list page marks the failed attempt distinctly, not just 'partial'\",\n365\t      \"adapter not reachable\" in r.text, \"'adapter not reachable' not in page body\")\n366\tcheck(\"the list page offers a per-scan Health report link\",\n367\t      f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/{NEWER_ID}/health\" in r.text,\n368\t      \"no Health report link for the newest scan\")\n369\tcheck(\"the list page offers a compare picker (two selects + a Compare button)\",\n370\t      '<select name=\"a\"' in r.text and '<select name=\"b\"' in r.text\n371\t      and \"Compare</button>\" in r.text,\n372\t      \"compare picker not found on the list page\")\n373\t\n374\tr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/{NEWER_ID}\")\n375\tcheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans/{id} page is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\n376\tcheck(\"the detail page shows the fuel_level freeze frame\",\n377\t      \"Fuel level\" in r.text, \"Fuel level not in page body\")\n378\tcheck(\"the detail page shows the Mode 06 FAIL chip\", \"FAIL\" in r.text, \"FAIL not in page body\")\n379\tcheck(\"the detail page shows its own coverage line\",\n380\t      \"IHS 2 modules\" in r.text, \"coverage line not on the detail page\")\n381\t# The nearest EARLIER scan to NEWER is the manual partial scan (18:40),\n382\t# not the older full scan (18:00) -- \"previous\" is nearest, not \"first\".\n383\tcheck(\"the detail page offers a compare-with-previous section, linking the \"\n384\t      \"nearest earlier scan\",\n385\t      PARTIAL_ID in r.text, \"nearest-previous scan id not linked from the detail page\")\n386\t\n387\tr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/SCAN_0000000000\")\n388\tcheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans/{unknown id} page is 404\", r.status_code == 404, str(r.status_code))\n389\t\n390\t\n391\t# --- the diff page, its own route ---------------------------------------------\n392\t\n393\tr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/diff\", params={\"a\": OLDER_ID, \"b\": NEWER_ID})\n394\tcheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans/diff is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\n395\tcheck(\"the diff page shows the added stored code\", \"P0440\" in r.text, r.text[:200])\n396\tcheck(\"the diff page shows the Mode 06 flip\", \"FAIL\" in r.text, r.text[:200])\n397\tcheck(\"the diff page shows the coverage change\", \"IHS 2 modules\" in r.text, r.text[:200])\n398\t\n399\tr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/diff\", params={\"a\": OLDER_ID, \"b\": \"SCAN_0000000000\"})\n400\tcheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans/diff with an unknown scan id is 404\",\n401\t      r.status_code == 404, str(r.status_code))\n402\t\n403\t\n404\tprint()\n405\tif failures:\n406\t    print(f\"{len(failures)}/{checks} check(s) failed:\")\n407\t    for f in failures:\n408\t        print(f\"  - {f}\")\n409\t    sys.exit(1)\n410\tprint(f\"all {checks} checks passed\")\n411\t"}]},"uuid":"9f7dedac-17c0-4f33-bf6b-a64f3a8cccba","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:58:47.631Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\tests\\check_scanlog.py","content":"\"\"\"Checks for the scan log (``cuore.live.scanlog``, ``cuore.services.scanlog_bridge``,\n``cuore.api.scanlog``, ``cuore.web.scanlog_routes``).\n\nAnswers the owner's question \"does CUORE have a log area to save the freeze\nframe data?\" -- it did not; this groups the from-car rows already appended\nto ``observations.jsonl`` into browsable scans on read. Nothing here is a\nsecond copy of the truth and nothing here opens COM3 or calls a live\nadapter endpoint: every observation below is a hand-built fixture appended\nstraight to a throwaway ``observations.jsonl`` (same posture as\n``cuore/tests/check_detail.py``/``check_dossier_view.py``), tagged with a\nreal ``stream=\"serial COM3@115200\"`` value so ``is_from_car`` accepts it the\nsame way a real bench read would.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore/tests/check_dossier_view.py``: ``CUORE_STATE_DIR``\npoints at a throwaway directory BEFORE cuore is imported, and this app's own\nrouter may not be wired into ``create_app()`` yet elsewhere in a concurrent\nedit -- it is included defensively if missing.\n\nRun:\n    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_scanlog.py\n    .venv/Scripts/python.exe cuore/tests/check_screens.py\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nos.environ[\"CUORE_STATE_DIR\"] = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"cuore-check-scanlog-\")\nos.environ.pop(\"CUORE_AUDIT_PATH\", None)\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]))\n\nfrom fastapi.testclient import TestClient  # noqa: E402\n\nfrom cuore.app import create_app  # noqa: E402\nfrom cuore.api import scanlog as scanlog_api  # noqa: E402\nfrom cuore.web import scanlog_routes  # noqa: E402\nfrom cuore.live import scanlog, store as live_store  # noqa: E402\nfrom cuore.services import scanlog_bridge  # noqa: E402\nfrom cuore.services.errors import NotFound  # noqa: E402\n\nVIN = \"ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\"  # the Stelvio -- real VIN used across this suite's fixtures\n\nfailures: list[str] = []\nchecks = 0\n\n\ndef check(label: str, cond: bool, detail: str = \"\") -> None:\n    global checks\n    checks += 1\n    mark = \"ok\" if cond else \"FAIL\"\n    print(f\"  [{mark}] {label}\" + (f\" -- {detail}\" if detail and not cond else \"\"))\n    if not cond:\n        failures.append(label)\n\n\napp = create_app()\nexisting_paths = {getattr(r, \"path\", None) for r in app.routes}\nif \"/api/scans/{vin}\" not in existing_paths:\n    app.include_router(scanlog_api.router, prefix=\"/api\")\nif \"/v/{vin}/scans\" not in existing_paths:\n    app.include_router(scanlog_routes.router)\nclient = TestClient(app)\n\n\ndef _write(at: datetime, kind: str, data: dict, *, vin: str = \"\",\n          stream: str = \"serial COM3@115200\") -> None:\n    entry = {\"at\": at.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"), \"kind\": kind, \"vin\": vin,\n             \"bus\": \"can_c\", \"cable\": \"none\", \"stream\": stream, \"data\": data}\n    with live_store.observations_path().open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        f.write(json.dumps(entry) + \"\\n\")\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# Fixture: one older, clean scan; one newer scan with findings; one\n# demo/replay row that must never surface as a scan of its own.\n# ===========================================================================\n\nOLDER = datetime(2026, 10, 13, 18, 0, 0)\n_write(OLDER, \"obd_dtcs\", {\"kind\": \"stored\", \"dtcs\": [], \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": []}})\n_write(OLDER + timedelta(minutes=1), \"readiness\",\n      {\"since_clear\": {\"mil_on\": False, \"stored_dtc_count\": 0,\n                        \"monitors\": [{\"monitor\": \"Evaporative system\", \"supported\": True,\n                                      \"complete\": True}],\n                        \"all_complete\": True}}, vin=VIN)\n# A full/guided scan's own scan_coverage observation, same cluster (within\n# WINDOW of the readiness read above): CAN-C swept (5 modules answered),\n# IHS/CH never attempted -- the exact coverage line the owner's own spec\n# quotes.\n_write(OLDER + timedelta(minutes=2), \"scan_coverage\", {\n    \"scan_id\": \"SCAN_\" + OLDER.strftime(\"%y%m%d%H%M\"), \"vin\": VIN, \"cable\": \"none\",\n    \"buses_attempted\": [\"can_c\"], \"duration_s\": 12.0, \"steps\": [],\n    \"coverage\": [{\"bus\": \"can_c\", \"module\": m, \"category\": \"answered\", \"why\": None,\n                  \"active\": 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0}\n                for m in (\"ECM\", \"IPC\", \"TCM\", \"DTCM\", \"ESM\")],\n    \"counts\": {\"active\": 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0},\n}, vin=VIN)\n\n# A demo/replay read, timestamped well clear of either real window (>15 min\n# from both), tagged with a non-serial stream -- is_from_car() must reject\n# it outright, so it must never become a scan, and P9999 must never appear\n# anywhere in the scan log.\n_write(OLDER + timedelta(hours=1), \"obd_dtcs\", {\"kind\": \"stored\", \"dtcs\": [\"P9999\"]},\n      vin=VIN, stream=\"demo\")\n\n# A manual, single-purpose read (Codes/Live/Tests, not a guided/full scan)\n# more than 15 min clear of both real windows -- its own \"partial\" scan:\n# still a scan (counted by scan_plan), but with no scan_coverage observation\n# at all.\nPARTIAL = OLDER + timedelta(minutes=40)\n_write(PARTIAL, \"freeze_frame\",\n      {\"pid\": \"02\", \"name\": None, \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": {\"dtc\": \"P0128\", \"bytes\": [\"00\", \"00\"]}}},\n      vin=VIN)\nPARTIAL_ID = PARTIAL.strftime(scanlog.ID_FMT)\n\nNEWER = datetime(2026, 10, 13, 20, 0, 0)\n_write(NEWER, \"obd_dtcs\",\n      {\"kind\": \"stored\", \"dtcs\": [\"P0440\"], \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": [\"P0440\"]}})\n_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=3), \"obd_dtcs\",\n      {\"kind\": \"pending\", \"dtcs\": [\"P0455\"], \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": [\"P0455\"]}})\n_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=6), \"readiness\",\n      {\"since_clear\": {\"mil_on\": True, \"stored_dtc_count\": 1,\n                        \"monitors\": [{\"monitor\": \"Evaporative system\", \"supported\": True,\n                                      \"complete\": True}],\n                        \"all_complete\": True}}, vin=VIN)\n_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=9), \"mode06\",\n      {\"results\": {\"3A\": {\"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": [\n          {\"mid\": \"3A\", \"mid_name\": \"EVAP leak monitor\", \"tid\": \"91\", \"uasid\": \"30\",\n           \"unit\": \"ms\", \"value\": 100, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 50, \"passed\": False}]}}},\n       \"evap_summary\": [\"EVAP leak monitor: value 100 ms vs limit 50 ms -> FAIL\"]}, vin=VIN)\n_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=12), \"freeze_frame\",\n      {\"pid\": \"02\", \"name\": None, \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": {\"dtc\": \"P0440\", \"bytes\": [\"00\", \"00\"]}}})\n_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=13), \"freeze_frame\",\n      {\"pid\": \"2F\", \"name\": \"fuel_level\",\n       \"by_ecu\": {\"18DAF110\": {\"pid\": \"2F\", \"name\": \"fuel_level\", \"bytes\": [\"6B\"],\n                                \"unit\": \"%\", \"value\": 42.0}}})\n# A guided scan: CAN-C (6 modules, one ACTIVE) and CAN-IHS (2 modules) swept,\n# CAN-CH never attempted.\n_write(NEWER + timedelta(minutes=14), \"scan_coverage\", {\n    \"scan_id\": \"SCAN_\" + NEWER.strftime(\"%y%m%d%H%M\"), \"vin\": VIN, \"cable\": \"blue_a5\",\n    \"buses_attempted\": [\"can_c\", \"can_ihs\"], \"duration_s\": 40.0, \"steps\": [],\n    \"coverage\": ([{\"bus\": \"can_c\", \"module\": m, \"category\": \"answered\", \"why\": None,\n                  \"active\": 1 if m == \"ECM\" else 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0}\n                 for m in (\"ECM\", \"IPC\", \"TCM\", \"DTCM\", \"ESM\", \"BCM\")]\n                + [{\"bus\": \"can_ihs\", \"module\": m, \"category\": \"answered\", \"why\": None,\n                   \"active\": 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0}\n                  for m in (\"RFHUB\", \"DASM\")]),\n    \"counts\": {\"active\": 1, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0},\n    \"guided\": True, \"guided_status\": \"done\",\n}, vin=VIN)\n\nNEWER_ID = NEWER.strftime(scanlog.ID_FMT)\nOLDER_ID = OLDER.strftime(scanlog.ID_FMT)\n\n# A failed full-scan attempt (2026-10-14 honesty fix): a scan_coverage\n# observation exists -- this WAS a fullscan/guided attempt, not a manual\n# read -- but every row is \"not_reachable\" (adapter/cable error, e.g.\n# COM3 failing to open): no module answered on any bus. Placed well\n# before OLDER so it stays the OLDEST scan and never disturbs \"newest\"\n# (NEWER_ID) in the checks below.\nATTEMPT = OLDER - timedelta(hours=2)\n_write(ATTEMPT, \"scan_coverage\", {\n    \"scan_id\": \"SCAN_\" + ATTEMPT.strftime(\"%y%m%d%H%M\"), \"vin\": VIN, \"cable\": \"none\",\n    \"buses_attempted\": [\"can_c\"], \"duration_s\": 1.0, \"steps\": [],\n    \"coverage\": [{\"bus\": \"can_c\", \"module\": m, \"category\": \"not_reachable\",\n                 \"why\": \"LinkUnavailable: could not open COM3\", \"active\": 0,\n                 \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0}\n                for m in (\"ECM\", \"IPC\", \"TCM\", \"DTCM\", \"ESM\")],\n    \"counts\": {\"active\": 0, \"history\": 0, \"not_run\": 0},\n}, vin=VIN)\nATTEMPT_ID = ATTEMPT.strftime(scanlog.ID_FMT)\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# cuore.live.scanlog -- direct\n# ===========================================================================\n\nscans = scanlog.list_scans(VIN)\ncheck(\"exactly 4 scans are grouped for this VIN (attempt, older, partial, newer)\",\n      len(scans) == 4, str(len(scans)))\ncheck(\"newest scan listed first\", bool(scans) and scans[0][\"id\"] == NEWER_ID,\n      str([s[\"id\"] for s in scans]))\ncheck(\"no scan carries the demo-stream P9999 code\",\n      not any(\"P9999\" in s[\"dtcs\"][\"stored\"] for s in scans), str(scans))\n\nnewest = scanlog.get_scan(VIN, NEWER_ID)\ncheck(\"newest scan found by id\", newest is not None)\nif newest:\n    check(\"newest scan has stored P0440\", newest[\"dtcs\"][\"stored\"] == [\"P0440\"],\n          str(newest[\"dtcs\"]))\n    check(\"newest scan has pending P0455\", newest[\"dtcs\"][\"pending\"] == [\"P0455\"],\n          str(newest[\"dtcs\"]))\n    check(\"MIL is on\", newest[\"mil\"] is True, str(newest[\"mil\"]))\n\n    mode06_3a = next((r for r in newest[\"mode06\"] if r[\"mid\"] == \"3A\"), None)\n    check(\"Mode 06 3A is present\", mode06_3a is not None, str(newest[\"mode06\"]))\n    check(\"Mode 06 3A FAILed\", bool(mode06_3a) and mode06_3a[\"passed\"] is False,\n          str(mode06_3a))\n\n    ff = next((f for f in newest[\"freeze_frames\"] if f[\"code\"] == \"P0440\"), None)\n    check(\"a P0440 freeze frame is present\", ff is not None, str(newest[\"freeze_frames\"]))\n    fuel = next((p for p in (ff or {}).get(\"pids\", []) if p[\"pid\"] == \"2F\"), None)\n    check(\"the freeze frame lists the fuel_level PID\", fuel is not None, str(ff))\n    check(\"its name is sentence-cased\", bool(fuel) and fuel[\"name\"] == \"Fuel level\",\n          str(fuel))\n    check(\"its value round-trips\", bool(fuel) and fuel[\"value\"] == 42.0, str(fuel))\n\nolder = scanlog.get_scan(VIN, OLDER_ID)\ncheck(\"older scan found by id\", older is not None)\nif older:\n    check(\"older scan has no stored codes\", older[\"dtcs\"][\"stored\"] == [], str(older[\"dtcs\"]))\n    check(\"older scan is not partial (it has a scan_coverage observation)\",\n          older[\"partial\"] is False, str(older[\"partial\"]))\n    check(\"older scan's status is 'complete' (CAN-C answered modules)\",\n          older[\"status\"] == \"complete\", str(older[\"status\"]))\n    check(\"older scan's coverage line matches the owner's own spec wording\",\n          older[\"coverage\"][\"line\"] ==\n          \"CAN-C 5 modules · IHS not scanned (blue A5) · CH not scanned (grey A6)\",\n          str((older.get(\"coverage\") or {}).get(\"line\")))\n\ncheck(\"newest scan's coverage shows the IHS pass (guided scan)\",\n      bool(newest) and \"IHS 2 modules\" in (newest[\"coverage\"] or {}).get(\"line\", \"\"),\n      str((newest or {}).get(\"coverage\")))\ncheck(\"newest scan is not partial\", bool(newest) and newest[\"partial\"] is False)\ncheck(\"newest scan's status is 'complete'\", bool(newest) and newest[\"status\"] == \"complete\",\n      str((newest or {}).get(\"status\")))\n\npartial = scanlog.get_scan(VIN, PARTIAL_ID)\ncheck(\"the manual freeze-panel-only scan is found by id\", partial is not None)\nif partial:\n    check(\"it has no scan_coverage observation -> coverage is None\",\n          partial[\"coverage\"] is None, str(partial[\"coverage\"]))\n    check(\"it is labelled partial\", partial[\"partial\"] is True, str(partial[\"partial\"]))\n    check(\"its status is 'partial', not 'attempt' (never ran a bus sweep at all)\",\n          partial[\"status\"] == \"partial\", str(partial[\"status\"]))\n\nattempt = scanlog.get_scan(VIN, ATTEMPT_ID)\ncheck(\"the failed full-scan attempt is found by id\", attempt is not None)\nif attempt:\n    check(\"it has a scan_coverage observation (it WAS a bus-sweep attempt)\",\n          attempt[\"coverage\"] is not None, str(attempt[\"coverage\"]))\n    check(\"its status is 'attempt' (no module answered on any bus)\",\n          attempt[\"status\"] == \"attempt\", str(attempt[\"status\"]))\n    check(\"it is still marked partial for display purposes (not a complete scan)\",\n          attempt[\"partial\"] is True, str(attempt[\"partial\"]))\n\ncheck(\"unknown scan id resolves to None\", scanlog.get_scan(VIN, \"SCAN_0000000000\") is None)\ncheck(\"a different VIN sees no scans\", scanlog.list_scans(\"UNKNOWNVIN0000000\") == [])\n\n\n# --- scan plan (the \"Scan n of 10\" chip) --------------------------------------\n# 2026-10-14 honesty fix: only a COMPLETE scan counts -- the manual partial\n# read and the failed COM3 attempt do not, so of the 4 scans on file only\n# OLDER and NEWER (both complete) count toward \"Scan n of 10\".\n\nplan = scanlog.scan_plan(VIN)\ncheck(\"scan_plan counts only COMPLETE scans (2 of 4 -- the manual partial \"\n      \"read and the failed attempt don't count)\",\n      plan == {\"count\": 2, \"total\": 10}, str(plan))\ncheck(\"a vehicle with no scans plans 0 of 10\",\n      scanlog.scan_plan(\"UNKNOWNVIN0000000\") == {\"count\": 0, \"total\": 10})\n\n\n# --- diff --------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nd = scanlog.diff(VIN, OLDER_ID, NEWER_ID)\ncheck(\"diff between the two scans exists\", d is not None)\nif d:\n    check(\"diff reports P0440 added (stored)\", d[\"codes\"][\"stored\"][\"added\"] == [\"P0440\"],\n          str(d[\"codes\"]))\n    check(\"diff reports a Mode 06 3A change\", any(c[\"mid\"] == \"3A\" for c in d[\"mode06_changes\"]),\n          str(d[\"mode06_changes\"]))\n    check(\"diff reports a readiness/MIL change\",\n          any(c[\"monitor\"] == \"MIL\" for c in d[\"readiness_changes\"]),\n          str(d[\"readiness_changes\"]))\n    check(\"diff reports the coverage change (IHS now swept)\",\n          bool(d[\"coverage_changes\"]) and \"IHS 2 modules\" in d[\"coverage_changes\"][0][\"after\"],\n          str(d[\"coverage_changes\"]))\n    check(\"diff reports no status_changes between these two (no code moved bucket)\",\n          d[\"status_changes\"] == [], str(d[\"status_changes\"]))\ncheck(\"diff against an unknown scan id returns None\", scanlog.diff(VIN, OLDER_ID, \"SCAN_x\") is None)\n\n\n# --- MES export ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nmes_text = scanlog.export_mes_text(newest)\n# cuore.bootstrap (imported as a side effect of cuore.app, above) already put\n# mes-log-mcp's own \"mes\" package on sys.path -- the one place that happens,\n# per that module's own docstring.\nfrom mes import scan as mes_scan  # noqa: E402\n\nparsed = mes_scan.parse_scan_text(mes_text, name=f\"{NEWER_ID}.txt\")\nall_codes = {d.code for d in parsed.all_dtcs}\ncheck(\"the MES export parses\", parsed is not None)\ncheck(\"the MES export's codes include P0440\", \"P0440\" in all_codes, str(all_codes))\ncheck(\"the MES export's codes include P0455\", \"P0455\" in all_codes, str(all_codes))\n\nwritten = scanlog.write_mes_export(VIN, NEWER_ID)\ncheck(\"write_mes_export wrote under CUORE_STATE_DIR/scans/<vin>/, never MES's own folder\",\n      written is not None and \"scans\" in written.parts and VIN in written.parts,\n      str(written))\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# cuore.services.scanlog_bridge\n# ===========================================================================\n\ntry:\n    scanlog_bridge.scan(VIN, \"SCAN_0000000000\")\n    check(\"bridge raises NotFound for an unknown scan id\", False)\nexcept NotFound:\n    check(\"bridge raises NotFound for an unknown scan id\", True)\n\nexport_json = scanlog_bridge.export(VIN, NEWER_ID, \"json\")\ncheck(\"bridge json export carries the scan's own id\",\n      export_json[\"content\"][\"id\"] == NEWER_ID, str(export_json[\"content\"].get(\"id\")))\nexport_mes = scanlog_bridge.export(VIN, NEWER_ID, \"mes\")\ncheck(\"bridge mes export is text containing the stored code\",\n      \"P0440\" in export_mes[\"content\"], export_mes[\"content\"][:200])\n\ncheck(\"bridge scan_plan matches cuore.live.scanlog.scan_plan\",\n      scanlog_bridge.scan_plan(VIN) == {\"count\": 2, \"total\": 10},\n      str(scanlog_bridge.scan_plan(VIN)))\n\n\n# ===========================================================================\n# HTTP: TestClient only, never COM3 / a live adapter endpoint\n# ===========================================================================\n\nr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}\")\ncheck(\"GET /api/scans/{vin} is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\ncheck(\"it lists all 4 scans\", len(r.json()[\"scans\"]) == 4, str(r.json()))\n\nr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/{NEWER_ID}\")\ncheck(\"GET /api/scans/{vin}/{id} is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\n\nr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/diff\", params={\"a\": OLDER_ID, \"b\": NEWER_ID})\ncheck(\"GET /api/scans/{vin}/diff is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\ncheck(\"it reports P0440 added\", r.json()[\"codes\"][\"stored\"][\"added\"] == [\"P0440\"], str(r.json()))\n\nr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/{NEWER_ID}/export\", params={\"fmt\": \"json\"})\ncheck(\"export?fmt=json is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\nr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/{NEWER_ID}/export\", params={\"fmt\": \"mes\"})\ncheck(\"export?fmt=mes is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\ncheck(\"the mes export body round-trips through the real parser\",\n      \"P0440\" in {d.code for d in mes_scan.parse_scan_text(r.text).all_dtcs}, r.text[:200])\n\nr = client.get(f\"/api/scans/{VIN}/SCAN_0000000000\")\ncheck(\"GET of an unknown scan is 404\", r.status_code == 404, str(r.status_code))\n\nr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans\")\ncheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans page is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\ncheck(\"the list page shows the newest scan's stored code\",\n      \"P0440\" in r.text, \"P0440 not in page body\")\ncheck(\"the list page shows the scan plan chip (2 complete scans on file, out of 10)\",\n      \"Scan 2 of 10\" in r.text, \"'Scan 2 of 10' not in page body\")\ncheck(\"the list page marks the manual scan partial\",\n      \"partial\" in r.text, \"'partial' not in page body\")\ncheck(\"the list page marks the failed attempt distinctly, not just 'partial'\",\n      \"adapter not reachable\" in r.text, \"'adapter not reachable' not in page body\")\ncheck(\"the list page offers a per-scan Health report link\",\n      f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/{NEWER_ID}/health\" in r.text,\n      \"no Health report link for the newest scan\")\ncheck(\"the list page offers a compare picker (two selects + a Compare button)\",\n      '<select name=\"a\"' in r.text and '<select name=\"b\"' in r.text\n      and \"Compare</button>\" in r.text,\n      \"compare picker not found on the list page\")\n\nr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/{NEWER_ID}\")\ncheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans/{id} page is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\ncheck(\"the detail page shows the fuel_level freeze frame\",\n      \"Fuel level\" in r.text, \"Fuel level not in page body\")\ncheck(\"the detail page shows the Mode 06 FAIL chip\", \"FAIL\" in r.text, \"FAIL not in page body\")\ncheck(\"the detail page shows its own coverage line\",\n      \"IHS 2 modules\" in r.text, \"coverage line not on the detail page\")\n# The nearest EARLIER scan to NEWER is the manual partial scan (18:40),\n# not the older full scan (18:00) -- \"previous\" is nearest, not \"first\".\ncheck(\"the detail page offers a compare-with-previous section, linking the \"\n      \"nearest earlier scan\",\n      PARTIAL_ID in r.text, \"nearest-previous scan id not linked from the detail page\")\n\nr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/SCAN_0000000000\")\ncheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans/{unknown id} page is 404\", r.status_code == 404, str(r.status_code))\n\n\n# --- the diff page, its own route ---------------------------------------------\n\nr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/diff\", params={\"a\": OLDER_ID, \"b\": NEWER_ID})\ncheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans/diff is 200\", r.status_code == 200, str(r.status_code))\ncheck(\"the diff page shows the added stored code\", \"P0440\" in r.text, r.text[:200])\ncheck(\"the diff page shows the Mode 06 flip\", \"FAIL\" in r.text, r.text[:200])\ncheck(\"the diff page shows the coverage change\", \"IHS 2 modules\" in r.text, r.text[:200])\n\nr = client.get(f\"/v/{VIN}/scans/diff\", params={\"a\": OLDER_ID, \"b\": \"SCAN_0000000000\"})\ncheck(\"GET /v/{vin}/scans/diff with an unknown scan id is 404\",\n      r.status_code == 404, str(r.status_code))\n\n\nprint()\nif failures:\n    print(f\"{len(failures)}/{checks} check(s) failed:\")\n    for f in failures:\n        print(f\"  - {f}\")\n    sys.exit(1)\nprint(f\"all {checks} checks passed\")\n","numLines":411,"startLine":1,"totalLines":411}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8135d8bd-ee29-4729-832b-43e119999e83","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"9f7dedac-17c0-4f33-bf6b-a64f3a8cccba","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7f5dba9e9d416cc6","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg2QWJkS6g9oEhLetv2bB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BPzeom2XHMAmbxUAsWR4gX","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\vehicles\\ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\\reports\\2026-10-13-scan-health-report.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9003,"cache_read_input_tokens":57019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9003,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BPzeom2XHMAmbxUAsWR4gX":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\vehicles\\ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\\reports\\2026-10-13-scan-health-report.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"58723456-c990-452f-99b1-657b43873c16","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011Cg2QWJVYr7DziFqH7AZXp","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad1a8f69-199a-4103-9f56-2eb430b5fecf","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:58:48.642Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"ad1a8f69-199a-4103-9f56-2eb430b5fecf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4f6844c0-3b82-41b2-99e4-abe62041f502","agentId":"a7f5dba9e9d416cc6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BPzeom2XHMAmbxUAsWR4gX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Scan health report — 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T, VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\n2\t\n3\tAs of 2026-10-13 20:04, read live from the car (serial COM3, vLinker FS r2 / STN1170, 29-bit legislated OBD; ECM 18DAF110, TCM 18DAF118). Engine idling, 752–778 rpm, coolant 101 °C, 14.1 V at the port. Odometer about 142 290 km. Source files: `sessions/2026-10-13-live-read.json`, observation store (from-car). Confidence grades: CONFIRMED (manufacturer document), CORROBORATED (two sources), SINGLE-SOURCE, UNKNOWN (use the service manual, TechAuthority). Nothing below is invented; where a Stelvio specification is not on file the reading is reported without a verdict.\n4\t\n5\t## Verdict\n6\t\n7\t**ACTIVE FAULT — EVAP.** MIL on. Stored P0440; pending P0440 + P0455; permanent P0440 + P0456. Every readiness monitor has completed since the 29 Sep clear (1 663 km, 8 warm-ups), so the EVAP monitor has run with fuel in its window and the code came back: this is no longer \"unverified repair\", it is a live fault with a measured failure behind it (below). Everything else the ECM measures passes.\n8\t\n9\t## System by system\n10\t\n11\t| System | Reading | Band / spec | Health |\n12\t|---|---|---|---|\n13\t| EVAP | Mode 06: gross-leak test PASS; **0.090\" large-leak test FAIL, 404 ms vs ≥ 3 965 ms**; 0.020\" small-leak TID 90 FAIL 6 096 vs ≤ 6 000 (1.6 % over); purge-flow tests PASS (168 in 57–328). Freeze frame: purge commanded 18 %, fuel 28.6 %, 217 s after start, ECT 63 °C, idle 778 rpm | ECM's own limits (CONFIRMED, read from the car) | **FAULT** |\n14\t| Fuel & air (closed loop) | Frame: STFT +3.1 %, LTFT −2.3 %, λ 1.007. Hot idle: STFT +3.1 %, LTFT −5.5 %, λ 1.007, MAF 3.24 g/s, MAP 31 kPa at baro 98 kPa (≈ 67 kPa idle vacuum), load 19.6 % | Trims ±10 % (CORROBORATED). Idle MAF/MAP for the GME 2.0T: UNKNOWN | OK — trims inside band, strong idle vacuum, no sign of an intake leak |\n15\t| Ignition / misfire | Mode 06 misfire counters 0–1 per cylinder, all PASS. Timing +5° at hot idle, −4.5° in the cold frame (catalyst-heating retard, SINGLE-SOURCE engineering practice) | ECM limits (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n16\t| Catalyst | MID 21: 5 700 vs ≥ 1 764 — PASS, 3.2× margin | ECM limit (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n17\t| Oxygen sensors | MID 02 all PASS: downstream 913 mV, response 592 / 320 ms within limits; MID 41/42 PASS | ECM limits (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n18\t| VVT / MultiAir | MID 35: all 12 tests PASS | ECM limits (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n19\t| EGR (as reported by the ECM) | MID 31 PASS | ECM limits (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n20\t| Cooling | 101 °C at idle after 30 min; ambient 25 °C (sensor), 17 °C in the frame | Hot-idle target for this engine: UNKNOWN | Reading only — plausible for a hot idle; confirm fan cycling and the manual's target |\n21\t| Charging / electrical | 14.0 V module voltage, 14.1 V at the port, idle | 13.5–14.7 V (CORROBORATED) | OK |\n22\t| Turbo / boost | Not exercised at idle (MAP 48 kPa at 13 % throttle in the frame) | — | Not assessed |\n23\t| Transmission (TCM 18DAF118) | Answers; no emissions codes (Mode 03/07/0A empty) | — | No OBD fault; UDS module read not done |\n24\t| Engine oil | PID 5C not supported by this ECM; IAT (0F) gave no data in this read | — | UNKNOWN — re-read IAT; oil temp needs a UDS DID |\n25\t| Body / chassis / network | Not read tonight (UDS module scan not run); B1176 and the 28 Sep network event unchecked | — | GAP |\n26\t\n27\t## What the EVAP measurement tells us\n28\t\n29\tThe ECM declares a large leak when its switch (ESIM) does not report the system sealed within the test time. Tonight it held for **0.4 s where ≥ 4 s is required**, with purge commanded at 18 % during a warm-up idle. Three smoke tests already found the system physically sealed and every EVAP part is new. The two explanations left are exactly the two on the hypothesis ledger: the ESIM switch / its signal path never reporting \"sealed\", or the ECM calibration (TSB 18-030-17 REV. B). The marginal 0.020\" result (6 096 vs 6 000) is consistent with the permanent P0456 and does not change that picture.\n30\t\n31\t## Issues to address, in order\n32\t\n33\t1. **Test A now** (hand vacuum on the ESIM while watching the switch PID) — it separates \"switch never closes\" from \"ECM never sees it\". Do not clear codes before it.\n34\t2. **wiTECH flash comparison** against TSB 18-030-17 REV. B; recalls 25V586000 and 18V636000 by VIN; TSB 21-035-20 (TCM).\n35\t3. **Run the UDS module scan** (BCM, gateway, chassis modules) for body/network codes — B1176 (rear-left window riser) and the 28 Sep lost-communication family are unverified tonight.\n36\t4. **Re-read IAT (PID 0F)** and take an oil-temperature DID; both came back empty.\n37\t5. Maintenance overdue by the manual (unchanged, service ledger still empty): transfer-case oil, drive belt; air filter and plugs due at 90 k mi; brake fluid 2-year interval.\n38\t6. Record this scan's freeze frame and Mode 06 as evidence on the EVAP hypotheses (CUORE now offers them in the picker; the mechanic attaches).\n39\t\n40\t## Clean bill tonight\n41\t\n42\tFuel control, ignition, catalyst, oxygen sensors, VVT, charging: all pass the ECM's own tests with margin. No misfire history. Idle vacuum strong. The car's problem is one system, and it is now measured, not inferred.\n43\t"}]},"uuid":"97e5f901-f68a-4b8e-8840-22ea4f3aaa24","timestamp":"2026-10-14T15:58:48.942Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\vehicles\\ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\\reports\\2026-10-13-scan-health-report.md","content":"# Scan health report — 2018 Alfa Romeo Stelvio 2.0T, VIN ZASFAKPN5J7B88115\n\nAs of 2026-10-13 20:04, read live from the car (serial COM3, vLinker FS r2 / STN1170, 29-bit legislated OBD; ECM 18DAF110, TCM 18DAF118). Engine idling, 752–778 rpm, coolant 101 °C, 14.1 V at the port. Odometer about 142 290 km. Source files: `sessions/2026-10-13-live-read.json`, observation store (from-car). Confidence grades: CONFIRMED (manufacturer document), CORROBORATED (two sources), SINGLE-SOURCE, UNKNOWN (use the service manual, TechAuthority). Nothing below is invented; where a Stelvio specification is not on file the reading is reported without a verdict.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**ACTIVE FAULT — EVAP.** MIL on. Stored P0440; pending P0440 + P0455; permanent P0440 + P0456. Every readiness monitor has completed since the 29 Sep clear (1 663 km, 8 warm-ups), so the EVAP monitor has run with fuel in its window and the code came back: this is no longer \"unverified repair\", it is a live fault with a measured failure behind it (below). Everything else the ECM measures passes.\n\n## System by system\n\n| System | Reading | Band / spec | Health |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| EVAP | Mode 06: gross-leak test PASS; **0.090\" large-leak test FAIL, 404 ms vs ≥ 3 965 ms**; 0.020\" small-leak TID 90 FAIL 6 096 vs ≤ 6 000 (1.6 % over); purge-flow tests PASS (168 in 57–328). Freeze frame: purge commanded 18 %, fuel 28.6 %, 217 s after start, ECT 63 °C, idle 778 rpm | ECM's own limits (CONFIRMED, read from the car) | **FAULT** |\n| Fuel & air (closed loop) | Frame: STFT +3.1 %, LTFT −2.3 %, λ 1.007. Hot idle: STFT +3.1 %, LTFT −5.5 %, λ 1.007, MAF 3.24 g/s, MAP 31 kPa at baro 98 kPa (≈ 67 kPa idle vacuum), load 19.6 % | Trims ±10 % (CORROBORATED). Idle MAF/MAP for the GME 2.0T: UNKNOWN | OK — trims inside band, strong idle vacuum, no sign of an intake leak |\n| Ignition / misfire | Mode 06 misfire counters 0–1 per cylinder, all PASS. Timing +5° at hot idle, −4.5° in the cold frame (catalyst-heating retard, SINGLE-SOURCE engineering practice) | ECM limits (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n| Catalyst | MID 21: 5 700 vs ≥ 1 764 — PASS, 3.2× margin | ECM limit (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n| Oxygen sensors | MID 02 all PASS: downstream 913 mV, response 592 / 320 ms within limits; MID 41/42 PASS | ECM limits (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n| VVT / MultiAir | MID 35: all 12 tests PASS | ECM limits (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n| EGR (as reported by the ECM) | MID 31 PASS | ECM limits (CONFIRMED) | OK |\n| Cooling | 101 °C at idle after 30 min; ambient 25 °C (sensor), 17 °C in the frame | Hot-idle target for this engine: UNKNOWN | Reading only — plausible for a hot idle; confirm fan cycling and the manual's target |\n| Charging / electrical | 14.0 V module voltage, 14.1 V at the port, idle | 13.5–14.7 V (CORROBORATED) | OK |\n| Turbo / boost | Not exercised at idle (MAP 48 kPa at 13 % throttle in the frame) | — | Not assessed |\n| Transmission (TCM 18DAF118) | Answers; no emissions codes (Mode 03/07/0A empty) | — | No OBD fault; UDS module read not done |\n| Engine oil | PID 5C not supported by this ECM; IAT (0F) gave no data in this read | — | UNKNOWN — re-read IAT; oil temp needs a UDS DID |\n| Body / chassis / network | Not read tonight (UDS module scan not run); B1176 and the 28 Sep network event unchecked | — | GAP |\n\n## What the EVAP measurement tells us\n\nThe ECM declares a large leak when its switch (ESIM) does not report the system sealed within the test time. Tonight it held for **0.4 s where ≥ 4 s is required**, with purge commanded at 18 % during a warm-up idle. Three smoke tests already found the system physically sealed and every EVAP part is new. The two explanations left are exactly the two on the hypothesis ledger: the ESIM switch / its signal path never reporting \"sealed\", or the ECM calibration (TSB 18-030-17 REV. B). The marginal 0.020\" result (6 096 vs 6 000) is consistent with the permanent P0456 and does not change that picture.\n\n## Issues to address, in order\n\n1. **Test A now** (hand vacuum on the ESIM while watching the switch PID) — it separates \"switch never closes\" from \"ECM never sees it\". Do not clear codes before it.\n2. **wiTECH flash comparison** against TSB 18-030-17 REV. B; recalls 25V586000 and 18V636000 by VIN; TSB 21-035-20 (TCM).\n3. **Run the UDS module scan** (BCM, gateway, chassis modules) for body/network codes — B1176 (rear-left window riser) and the 28 Sep lost-communication family are unverified tonight.\n4. **Re-read IAT (PID 0F)** and take an oil-temperature DID; both came back empty.\n5. Maintenance overdue by the manual (unchanged, service ledger still empty): transfer-case oil, drive belt; air filter and plugs due at 90 k mi; brake fluid 2-year interval.\n6. Record this scan's freeze frame and Mode 06 as evidence on the EVAP hypotheses (CUORE now offers them in the picker; the mechanic attaches).\n\n## Clean bill tonight\n\nFuel control, ignition, catalyst, oxygen sensors, VVT, charging: all pass the ECM's own tests with margin. No misfire history. Idle vacuum strong. The car's problem is one system, and it is now measured, not inferred.\n","numLines":43,"startLine":1,"totalLines":43}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad1a8f69-199a-4103-9f56-2eb430b5fecf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
